id\":\"atom::35253ee716d91b56449feb1f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该综述明确排除了肿瘤内微生物组（intratumoral microbiome），仅关注肠道微生物组的系统性影响。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s071\",\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::18e093e9c0650c0adb6a76bd\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"文中提到的临床关联多为观察性研究，不能直接推断因果关系；FMT等证据来自小规模概念验证试验，效力有限。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s071\",\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ea8815a44607a8b77c2201dc\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"所提机制多基于前临床模型，人体内的确切生理浓度和效应阈值尚不明确。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s071\",\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1be3f40b9e3ba9019333cb48\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"不同研究间的技术异质性和地理差异可能导致菌群-疗效关联的不一致性，需谨慎外推。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s071\",\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d4894969daf36d135d810ad5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"asset_id\":\"asset-b5c2e925a4132b88eff6\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-7f937d5566b4c12030ce\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"}],\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s071\",\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::349f23b247bb74e7f21b4e09\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"field_path\":[\"local_passages\"],\"value\":{\"external_calls\":0,\"passages\":[{\"best_sentence\":\"Landmark clinical and preclinical studies linking the gut microbiome to immune checkpoint inhibitor response and tumor microenvironment modulationImmune checkpoint inhibitor, NSCLC: Non-small cell lung cancer, RCC: Renal cell carcinoma, PFS/OS: Progression-free survival/overall survival, CTLA-4: cytotoxic T-lymphocyte-associated protein 4, FMT: Fecal microbiota transplantation, IFN: Interferon FMT from defined donors, and precision microbial consortia with ICI efficacy as primary endpoints, stratified by tumor immune phenotype.(3) Geographic diversity in study populations to establish generalizability across non-Western cohorts.(4) Longitudinal rather than single-baseline microbiome profiling to capture dynamic changes during ICI treatment.(5) Multivariate predictive modeling integrating microbiome functional data with tumor genomics, host immune profiling, and germline genetics.\",\"card_path\":\"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\paper_cards\\\\20260922_microbiome_batch\\\\reading\\\\cards\\\\9db1c1ced73dca207c6289b20b4a2914a09ca2b1\\\\0e352726189f698ed7200afeb2df9e1f\\\\attempt-01\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\",\"doi\":\"10.25259/ijmio_8_2026\",\"limits\":[],\"match_terms\":[\"粪菌移植\",\"gut microbiome modulate efficacy immune checkpoint inhibitors solid tumours\",\"ici\",\"nsclc\",\"rcc\"],\"material_depth\":\"fulltext\",\"paper_id\":\"9db1c1ced73dca207c6289b20b4a2914a09ca2b1\",\"pool_action\":\"already_in_pool\",\"reading_path\":\"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\paper_cards\\\\20260922_microbiome_batch\\\\materials\\\\9db1c1ced73dca207c6289b20b4a2914a09ca2b1\\\\snapshot-a22ccfd4fa2ec07e546e769c\",\"score\":45.119645,\"section_path\":[],\"segment_kind\":\"document_block\",\"source_handle\":\"P0363\",\"text\":\"Practical clinical considerations for microbiome-related interventions in patients receiving immune checkpoint inhibitors Landmark clinical and preclinical studies linking the gut microbiome to immune checkpoint inhibitor response and tumor microenvironment modulationImmune checkpoint inhibitor, NSCLC: Non-small cell lung cancer, RCC: Renal cell carcinoma, PFS/OS: Progression-free survival/overall survival, CTLA-4: cytotoxic T-lymphocyte-associated protein 4, FMT: Fecal microbiota transplantation, IFN: Interferon FMT from defined donors, and precision microbial consortia with ICI efficacy as primary endpoints, stratified by tumor immune phenotype.(3) Geographic diversity in study populations to establish generalizability across non-Western cohorts.(4) Longitudinal rather than single-baseline microbiome profiling to capture dynamic changes during ICI treatment.(5) Multivariate predictive modeling integrating microbiome functional data with tumor genomics, host immune profiling, and germline genetics. Artificial intelligence (AI)-assisted language tools were used during manuscript drafting and language refinement.All scientific content, interpretation, refere\",\"title\":\"The gut microbiome–tumor microenvironment axis in immunotherapy response: Mechanistic insights and clinical implications\",\"usable_fields\":[],\"year\":\"2026\"}],\"question\":\"How does the gut microbiome modulate the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in solid tumours, and what mechanisms mediate that effect? 微生物干预策略的临床转化现状 系统评估粪菌移植（FMT）、活体生物药（LBPs）、益生菌及饮食干预在实体瘤 ICI 治疗中的临床试验数据，区分初治与难治人群的疗效差异，明确证据等级（I/II 期 vs III 期），并分析供体选择、安全性及标准化挑战。 涵盖人体临床试验（I-III 期），聚焦实体瘤（黑色素瘤、NSCLC、RCC、CRC 等）。包括 FMT（供体来源、给药途径）、定义菌群（如 CBM588、MRx0518）、益生菌及饮食干预。明确排除纯临床前研究（除非用于解释机制背景）及非 ICI 背景的微生物干预。严格区分观察性关联与干预性因果证据，标注试验设计类型（单臂 vs RCT）及人群特征（初治 vs 经治）。\",\"reading_mode\":\"focused_local_search\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s047\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::fa917863b42b865823617a1e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"abstract\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4f68bc3c0e51d3eab948fccf\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ad5a28fe0d2f3d68b7b8e60f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"1. 数据收集：使用公开可用的418名NSCLC患者基线肠道微生物组物种谱数据。2. 模型构建：训练机器学习模型预测ICI响应（R vs NR），固定参数，在保留测试集上验证（AUC=0.62，OS曲线差异显著p<0.0001）。3. 筛选子集：聚焦于模型预测价值良好的257名患者。4. 模拟干预：在模型中模拟健康供体FMT和治疗性菌群组合添加到患者基线微生物组中的过程，考察不同定植比例（exposure-dependent）对预测响应概率的影响。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8dd8758eb8f26ba40de0493c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了一个基于基线微生物组预测ICI响应的机器学习框架，并证实了在特定患者亚群中，通过模拟FMT或定制菌群可提升预测响应率。\",\"limits\":\"所给摘要未交代具体的机器学习算法类型、特征选择细节、治疗性菌群的具体组成成分、菌株分离的具体进展以及临床转化的时间表。仅基于回顾性数据的模拟，非前瞻性临床试验结果。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::89e7cfb984cc8f88cb8a9ce6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"基于418名NSCLC患者数据的机器学习模型，在从未见过的测试集上\",\"finding\":\"模型平均AUC为0.62，能显著区分总生存期（OS）曲线（p<0.0001）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::93a5dccbe3d93c3c7257faa4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"在模型预测价值良好的257名患者子集中，模拟健康供体FMT添加\",\"finding\":\"FMT提高了模型预测的响应率，且效果依赖于暴露量（即FMT物种定植并替换患者基线微生物组的比例）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a54ca17131fe904ae7af49e9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"在相同子集中，模拟候选治疗性菌群组合添加\",\"finding\":\"候选治疗性菌群组合同样提高了响应率，且结果也呈现剂量/定植依赖性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::679f65a7a246700078865033\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"empirical\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b5b1d19764f6694dbdc7af78\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"现有研究中单个微生物物种与ICI响应的关联往往不可重复且统计效力不足；虽然FMT显示有益，但药物开发多集中于简单菌群组合。本研究试图在模型中复制FMT的治疗益处，并设计能够增强ICI响应的治疗性微生物组合。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ae8542404f12e8b138fd3320\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"基于418名非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者的基线肠道微生物组数据，构建机器学习模型以预测免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）的响应情况；并在模拟环境中评估粪菌移植（FMT）及设计型活细菌疗法对ICI疗效的影响。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4ae34442850db6176f0dc26c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"该研究旨在解决个体微生物物种与ICI响应关联缺乏统计稳健性的问题，并探索通过微生物组干预改善ICI疗效的策略。作者利用418名NSCLC患者的基线微生物组数据训练了一个区分响应者（R）与非响应者（NR）的机器学习模型（AUC=0.62）。随后，在具有良好预测价值的子集（n=257）中，通过模拟实验评估了健康供体FMT和自定义治疗性菌群组合的效果。结果显示，增加FMT或治疗性菌群的定植比例可依赖性地提高模型预测的响应率。结论认为这些候选疗法有潜力改善ICI患者响应，目前正进行菌株分离培养以开发联合疗法。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::52690f071bd7b697f8226c7c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该论文提供了关于“微生物组介导ICI疗效”的一个具体计算生物学视角。它不侧重于单一机制的发现，而是提供了一个从微生物组特征到临床响应预测的建模流程，并展示了通过恢复“响应者样”微生物组特征（通过FMT或合成菌群）来改善预后的概念验证。这对于综述中讨论“如何通过调节微生物组增强ICI疗效”以及“预测生物标志物的开发”部分具有直接参考价值。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8ac1b1eac700149a344ed443\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"模型性能中等（AUC 0.62），且仅在NSCLC队列中验证，外推至其他实体瘤需谨慎。所给摘要未交代模型的可解释性（即哪些具体菌群驱动了预测）。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了基于全谱微生物组而非单一物种的ICI响应预测模型构建方法，并量化了模型性能（AUC 0.62）。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a23aef9604c65bbc592eb585\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"这是基于计算机模拟的结果，非体内或体外实验验证。所给摘要未交代具体的分子机制（如抗原呈递、炎症调节等），仅停留在表型预测层面。\",\"contribution\":\"提出了通过“恢复响应者样微生物组特征”来克服ICI无响应的设计策略，并通过模拟证明了FMT和定制菌群的潜在有效性。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9427443eb0fa7c8aa3845ea9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"418名NSCLC患者的基线微生物组数据及其与ICI响应的统计关联分析。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::caf5e2a920fd8e6427e41f2c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"候选治疗性菌群的设计逻辑（围绕供体FMT和ICI响应相关物种及机制）及菌株分离培养的进展。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::107cddc181c0ebe6140204b3\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该研究仅为摘要级别，所有关于“治疗性菌群”的具体成分、作用机制及临床前/临床数据均未知，不得推断其具体功效或安全性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::32be3241aa6be5e4aa9c6909\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"模型基于回顾性数据，模拟结果不代表真实临床疗效，需明确区分“预测模型中的响应率提升”与“实际患者生存获益”。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1b85f9454a1366e32d8300b8\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"研究对象限定为NSCLC，其微生物组特征可能与其他实体瘤不同，跨癌种推广需谨慎。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4c5791d22681d874f3bce1ab\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"作者声称的“promise”为初步概念验证，尚处于菌株分离和培养阶段，距离实际应用仍有距离。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::674ce0ddf3f79ba2358a5d60\",\"source_handle\":\"P0329\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"kind\":\"identity\",\"reason\":\"source identity was not independently verified\",\"status\":\"input_attributed\"},{\"kind\":\"coverage\",\"reason\":\"no complete research body was indexed\",\"status\":\"partial\"},{\"kind\":\"coverage\",\"reason\":\"only abstract or non-title snippets were available\",\"status\":\"partial\"}],\"material_scope\":\"abstract_only\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s101\",\"s135\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::1f6436d467e7e0b57e2f07b2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0357\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s025\",\"s109\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e1cc78c58c16c3bbdbbf2ee2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0357\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s025\",\"s109\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::00a19ae4aaf57c17faf6d44e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0357\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"采用系统性文献综合路线。首先梳理肠道微生物组调节局部及全身免疫的基础生物学机制（受体信号通路、表观遗传调控）。其次，分类汇总临床前研究（主要是小鼠模型），分析特定菌株对树突状细胞、T细胞极化及肿瘤微环境的影响。再次，系统检索并归纳人类临床研究数据，包括回顾性队列、前瞻性观察研究及I/II期临床试验，按癌种（肺癌、肾癌、黑色素瘤等）和治疗类型进行分层分析。最后，结合专家观点与现有文献缺口，提出整合多组学、体外功能 assay 及标准化临床试验的未来研究框架。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s025\",\"s109\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::71d806cb03a92d98e2986d9d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0357\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"提供了益生菌增强ICI疗效的多层次机制全景图，连接了微生物代谢物、免疫细胞亚群及肿瘤微环境重塑。\",\"limits\":\"机制部分主要基于小鼠模型，其外推至人类的适用性受限；人类数据多为观察性，存在选择偏倚和混杂因素。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s025\",\"s109\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9d832b25167ebcddca09a6b4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0357\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"系统整理了截至2025年的临床前及早期临床证据，揭示了不同癌种和益生菌类型的响应差异。\",\"limits\":\"临床数据异质性高，难以得出统一的疗效结论；缺乏长期安全性和长期定植效果的数据。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s025\",\"s109\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::33a9645f6cef26721b0123d6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0357\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"明确了当前领域的关键瓶颈（标准化缺失、监管障碍、因果推断困难），并为未来研究设计了方法论框架。\",\"limits\":\"作为综述，未提供新的原始实验数据；提出的未来方向需后续实证研究验证。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s025\",\"s109\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::302a80f9ec357636e98d3b23\",\"source_handle\":\"P0357\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"临床前小鼠模型（黑色素瘤、结直肠癌等）\",\"finding\":\"特定益生菌（如双歧杆菌、乳酸杆菌、Clostridium butyricum、Akkermansia muciniphila）可通过激活树突状细胞、促进MHC-I抗原呈递、调节细胞因子谱（增加IFN-γ, TNF-α）、诱导巨噬细胞向M1型极化以及产生SCFAs等代谢物，增强CD8+ T细胞浸润和活性，从而协同ICI发挥抗肿瘤作用。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s025\",\"s109\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0ff7bc74c4a0e8a80d1f6f4d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0357\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"人类回顾性及前瞻性观察研究（非小细胞肺癌、转移性肾细胞癌、黑色素瘤）\",\"finding\":\"多项研究显示，使用益生菌（尤其是Clostridium butyricum MIYAIRI 588或多种混合菌株）与改善无进展生存期（PFS）和总生存期（OS）相关。例如，在一项NSCLC回顾性研究中，益生菌使用者中位PFS显著延长；在mRCC的前瞻性研究中，CBM588联合nivolumab/ipilimumab显示出更高的客观缓解率（ORR）和PFS。然而，部分商业益生菌补充剂在非标准化使用时可能无效甚至有害。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s025\",\"s109\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3126473c4fbc3a92dfe180c6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0357\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）管理\",\"finding\":\"某些益生菌株（如Bifidobacterium spp., Lactobacillus spp.）在动物模型中可减轻ICI诱导的结肠炎。在人类观察性研究中，较高的有益菌丰度或与irAEs风险降低相关，但临床数据不一致，部分研究显示益生菌使用并未增加irAEs发生率，而在联合化疗时可能增加特定毒性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s025\",\"s109\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::30453997df29189781838b94\",\"source_handle\":\"P0357\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"方法学与标准化现状\",\"finding\":\"大多数临床证据来自回顾性研究，缺乏随机对照试验（RCT）。使用的益生菌制剂高度异质化（单株vs多株，商业补充剂vs定义明确的菌株），且受饮食、抗生素使用、种族等混杂因素影响严重。目前尚无法确定最佳菌株、剂量及给药方案。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s025\",\"s109\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::717397c1cb049347f7f2933f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0357\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s025\",\"s109\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::8c94036e7aec735063a13814\",\"source_handle\":\"P0357\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"尽管肠道微生物组已知能调节ICI疗效，但基于微生物组的干预措施（特别是益生菌）在临床实施中面临挑战。本研究旨在解决：1）益生菌如何通过具体免疫机制增强ICI疗效？2）目前关于益生菌在人类癌症患者中应用的临床证据质量如何？3）该领域存在哪些主要障碍（如标准化、安全性、混杂因素），需要何种研究设计来克服？\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s025\",\"s109\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7182dbc1a8c2edca834f2177\",\"source_handle\":\"P0357\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"聚焦于肠道微生物组（gut microbiome）与癌症免疫治疗，特别是免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）之间的相互作用。研究对象包括益生菌（probiotics）、益生元、后生元及粪便微生物移植等微生物靶向策略，涵盖从基础机制到临床前模型及早期临床试验的证据。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s025\",\"s109\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2e70d09ab215c701a9eb32bc\",\"source_handle\":\"P0357\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"本文是一篇综述，旨在批判性评估益生菌作为癌症免疫治疗辅助手段的现有证据。文章首先概述了肠道微生物组通过代谢物（如短链脂肪酸、色氨酸衍生物、胆汁酸）和分子模式调节宿主免疫系统的机制，进而阐述这些机制如何影响ICI疗效。随后，重点讨论了特定益生菌菌株在临床前小鼠模型中增强抗肿瘤免疫反应的潜力，并汇总了来自回顾性队列、前瞻性观察研究及早期临床试验的人类数据，探讨益生菌对ICI疗效及免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）的影响。最后，文章指出了当前研究的局限性，如菌株标准化缺失、混杂因素干扰及因果关系的未确定性，并提出了整合纵向多组学、体外共培养及类器官模型等未来研究方向，以推动益生菌从膳食补充剂向经过验证的临床辅助疗法转化。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s025\",\"s109\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::96cd7a2ea2aac507e2b78e97\",\"source_handle\":\"P0357\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该综述为理解肠道微生物组如何调节ICI疗效提供了全面的机制背景和临床证据汇总。对于综述规划，其核心价值在于：1）详细阐述了微生物代谢物（SCFAs, 色氨酸, 胆汁酸）及微生物模式（PAMPs/MAMPs）介导的具体免疫信号通路，可作为解释“机制”子问题的关键素材；2）提供了益生菌在不同实体瘤（NSCLC, RCC, Melanoma）中的临床观察数据对比，可用于分析“疗效异质性”及“菌株特异性”；3）指出了当前证据的局限性和未来研究方法学建议，有助于界定综述中关于“证据等级”和“研究空白”的讨论范围。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s025\",\"s109\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ebf057532e81f91a3c1deb34\",\"source_handle\":\"P0357\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"所有临床数据均为回顾性或早期前瞻性观察研究，存在显著的混杂因素（如基线微生物组成、饮食、合并用药）。不能直接证明因果关系，仅能提供关联证据。样本量和随访时间有限，长期疗效未知。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了益生菌在多种实体瘤（NSCLC, mRCC, 黑色素瘤）中与ICI联用的临床观察结果，包括PFS、OS和ORR的变化趋势。特别指出了Clostridium butyricum MIYAIRI 588在肺癌和肾癌中的积极信号，以及商业混合益生菌在某些情况下的无效性。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s025\",\"s109\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2151952a4c6ff4b033e7e506\",\"source_handle\":\"P0357\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"大部分机制细节源自小鼠模型（germ-free mice, gnotobiotic models）。人类体内确切的因果链条尚未完全确立，许多通路在人体中的确切贡献度和主导性尚不明确。不同菌株的作用机制可能存在显著差异，综述中的机制概括可能掩盖菌株特异性。\",\"contribution\":\"详细描述了益生菌调节免疫的具体分子和细胞机制：1）通过SCFAs激活GPCRs并抑制HDAC，促进Treg分化或增强CD8+ T细胞功能；2）通过AhR通路调节色氨酸代谢；3）通过STING通路激活DC和巨噬细胞，促进M1极化；4）通过分子模拟（molecular mimicry）交叉激活T细胞。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s025\",\"s109\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::4e3e5363e3b1e6060c91a4ba\",\"source_handle\":\"P0357\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"临床数据矛盾且不充分。动物模型结果不能直接外推至人类。缺乏大规模RCT数据支持益生菌对irAEs的确切保护作用。\",\"contribution\":\"分析了益生菌对ICI诱导的免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）的双向影响，指出某些菌株可能减轻结肠炎，而其他情况下可能增加毒性或无显著影响。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s025\",\"s109\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::bd22fb14494e0354503b38df\",\"source_handle\":\"P0357\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"介绍了肠道微生物组作为“第二基因组”的概念，及其通过GALT、代谢物和MAMPs调节全身免疫的基础理论。定义了益生菌、益生元、后生元和FMT的区别。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s025\",\"s109\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6830f3216aaff9dac057e352\",\"source_handle\":\"P0357\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"强调了当前临床研究中益生菌制剂的非标准化、商业产品的标签准确性问题、以及饮食/抗生素/种族等混杂因素的复杂性。提出了整合纵向多组学、ex vivo assays和gut-on-a-chip模型的必要性。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s025\",\"s109\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::114f3b3942444b88c43854a5\",\"source_handle\":\"P0357\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"引用Spencer等人的研究，显示非标准化的商业益生菌补充剂在小鼠模型和人类队列中可能损害ICI反应，减少IFN-γ阳性T细胞。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s025\",\"s109\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::960d60a84711ed898ae3e67f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0357\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该综述主要关注肠道微生物组，虽然提及皮肤、肺等其他部位微生物，但核心证据集中在肠道。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s025\",\"s109\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d798c8e48d06d32471513b4a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0357\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"临床数据主要来自回顾性研究和早期试点试验，缺乏大型III期RCT结果，因此任何关于疗效的结论都带有强烈的观察性关联性质，而非确证性因果证据。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s025\",\"s109\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::61e55c65ca40d7a2eecea481\",\"source_handle\":\"P0357\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"机制描述多基于小鼠模型，直接应用于人类需谨慎，因为人鼠微生物组和免疫系统存在差异。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s025\",\"s109\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::31ab31711e6241723cdfa314\",\"source_handle\":\"P0357\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"文中提到的“益生菌”涵盖从商业混合补充剂到定义明确的单一菌株（如CBM588），两者在成分、质量控制和潜在效果上截然不同，比较时需严格区分。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s025\",\"s109\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c16be694b7f8f95168cc4cea\",\"source_handle\":\"P0357\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"asset_id\":\"asset-d48cd64bd12b302ad2ba\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-76a4a344a1a9861e53c5\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-95bd9a77b14edf06222c\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"kind\":\"assets\",\"reason\":\"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\"status\":\"missing\"}],\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s025\",\"s109\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::297360b98d6705da27fdef6c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0273\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s033\",\"s023\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e3a4f29ae0327075e8a0f972\",\"source_handle\":\"P0273\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s033\",\"s267\",\"s023\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0eee6b0fc85c1aa61c7d0f69\",\"source_handle\":\"P0273\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"采用叙述性综述方法。电子数据库搜索策略包括关键词“cancer”、“immunotherapy/immune checkpoint inhibitor”和“microbiome/microbiota”。纳入标准限定为：成人（>18岁）、英文全文、同行评审期刊发表的研究。排除动物模型研究以专注于临床应用证据。对纳入的10项研究进行定性综合，按癌症类型（黑色素瘤、HCC、NSCLC等）和治疗结果（疗效、irAEs、FMT干预）分类整理发现。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s033\",\"s267\",\"s023\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f0e5381ebc2cc88f3e2bff9f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0273\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"首次专门针对临床研究的综述，汇总了肠道微生物组作为ICIs疗效预测生物标志物和irAEs风险因子的证据，强调了FMT在逆转耐药性方面的初步临床可行性。\",\"limits\":\"所纳入的研究样本量普遍较小（多数n≤42），存在异质性（不同癌症类型、不同ICI药物、不同测序方法如16S rRNA与宏基因组）。观察性研究无法确立因果关系。未对纳入的非随机研究进行严格的质量偏倚风险评估。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s033\",\"s267\",\"s023\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::cd1eb32400edde04370e97c2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0273\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"接受ICIs治疗的晚期癌症患者（黑色素瘤、HCC、NSCLC等）\",\"finding\":\"基线肠道微生物组的多样性和组成与ICIs疗效显著相关。高α-多样性通常与较长的PFS和OS相关。特定菌属富集与响应正相关（如Fecalibacterium prausnitzii, Bifidobacterium longum, Akkermansia muciniphila），而某些拟杆菌目（Bacteroidales）丰度高则与非响应相关。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s033\",\"s267\",\"s023\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::f5d7e1fba79b4eaef4b2e294\",\"source_handle\":\"P0273\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"接受CTLA-4抑制剂治疗的黑色素瘤患者\",\"finding\":\"低丰度的Bacteroidetes门细菌与免疫检查点抑制剂诱导的结肠炎（GI毒性）相关；相反，较高的Bacteroidetes丰度与抵抗结肠炎发生相关。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s033\",\"s267\",\"s023\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::10fa00141f5ccb618952ade4\",\"source_handle\":\"P0273\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"抗PD-1难治性转移性黑色素瘤患者接受来自响应者的FMT\",\"finding\":\"两项突破性临床试验显示，将来自免疫治疗响应者的粪菌移植给难治性患者，结合抗PD-1治疗，可使部分患者重新获得临床响应（Baruch et al. 3/10响应；Davar et al. 6/15响应），且安全性良好。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s033\",\"s267\",\"s023\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::322e6c1f1dc5e420331aed00\",\"source_handle\":\"P0273\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s033\",\"s267\",\"s023\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::3e9b4c255e7f49de211bb37f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0273\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"尽管免疫疗法提高了部分晚期癌症患者的生存率，但仅少数患者受益且常伴随严重免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）。目前尚缺乏基于临床证据的指导方针来利用肠道微生物组预测治疗反应或管理副作用。本研究试图厘清肠道微生物组作为预测生物标志物的潜力及其在增强疗效和减少副作用中的作用。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s033\",\"s267\",\"s023\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::da974f2fb7161247d30ad326\",\"source_handle\":\"P0273\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"临床癌症患者（晚期转移性黑色素瘤、肝细胞癌、非小细胞肺癌及肾细胞癌），聚焦于免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）治疗前后的肠道微生物组特征及其与疗效和不良事件的关系。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s033\",\"s267\",\"s023\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::39e920e15e0d4141f1858275\",\"source_handle\":\"P0273\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"该综述旨在评估肠道微生物组对癌症患者免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）临床结局及相关不良事件（AEs）的影响。作者检索了截至2021年3月的PubMed、Medline和ScienceDirect数据库，筛选出10项涉及成年人的临床研究。研究综合分析了基线微生物组的多样性（α/β多样性）和组成成分与ICIs疗效（无进展生存期PFS、总生存期OS）及胃肠道毒性（如结肠炎）之间的关联，并探讨了粪菌移植（FMT）在难治性患者中的潜在调节作用。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s033\",\"s267\",\"s023\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::e12c726d38ae415b29a4492d\",\"source_handle\":\"P0273\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"该论文提供了关于肠道微生物组如何影响实体瘤免疫治疗疗效的临床证据汇总，特别指出了特定菌群（如Faecalibacterium, Akkermansia）与疗效的正向关联，以及抗生素使用或特定菌群缺失与疗效不佳或毒性的关联。此外，它提供了FMT作为克服免疫耐药的临床干预案例，是讨论微生物组调控机制和临床转化潜力的重要素材。\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s033\",\"s267\",\"s023\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0539b1b2c53b3d7b72cb824c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0273\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"这些关联主要基于观察性研究，存在癌症类型异质性和样本量小的限制，不能直接推断因果机制。不同研究中具体差异菌种存在不一致性。\",\"contribution\":\"提供了多项临床研究数据，表明基线肠道微生物组的特定组成（如Faecalibacterium prausnitzii, Bifidobacterium longum, Akkermansia muciniphila的高丰度）和较高多样性与ICIs治疗的良好临床响应（延长PFS/OS）相关。同时指出Bacteroidales的高丰度与非响应相关。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s033\",\"s267\",\"s023\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::080e444842a4a14c522c5a13\",\"source_handle\":\"P0273\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"仅两项研究涉及此方面，且主要针对CTLA-4抑制剂，推广至其他ICI需谨慎。\",\"contribution\":\"揭示了肠道微生物组与免疫治疗不良反应（特别是结肠炎）的联系。低Bacteroidetes丰度与CTLA-4诱导的结肠炎风险增加相关。\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s033\",\"s267\",\"s023\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0fc5763ac32ca8ee7111a467\",\"source_handle\":\"P0273\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"样本量极小，仅为概念验证性质。供体和受体间的个体差异、预处理抗生素的使用等因素可能影响结果。尚未阐明具体的分子机制或关键菌株。\",\"contribution\":\"通过FMT临床试验（Baruch et al., Davar et al.）展示了从响应者向难治者移植微生物组可恢复部分患者的治疗响应，并观察到CD8+ T细胞激活增加和IL-8表达髓系细胞减少。这为微生物组介导免疫治疗效应的因果假设提供了最强的临床间接证据。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s033\",\"s267\",\"s023\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0151b710263ede70d23b60e6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0273\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"主要是相关性观察，未详细区分抗生素种类、使用时机及具体影响的菌群通路。\",\"contribution\":\"指出抗生素使用（尤其是ICIs期间）与较差的PFS和OS相关，提示抗生素引起的菌群失调可能是导致免疫治疗耐药的一个因素。\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s033\",\"s267\",\"s023\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::71bcf8d226c8b935ca4f2b4c\",\"source_handle\":\"P0273\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"综述指出目前尚无基于临床证据的指南来利用微生物组指导免疫治疗，且既往综述多包含动物模型，导致临床应用存在差距。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s033\",\"s267\",\"s023\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::327e635fac3256de3a41f1db\",\"source_handle\":\"P0273\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"提到现有研究在测序方法（16S vs 宏基因组）、样本采集时间点上的异质性，以及缺乏标准化的偏倚评估工具。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s033\",\"s267\",\"s023\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::89b7ba4679aef53d9192191a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0273\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"汇总了黑色素瘤、HCC、NSCLC中不同的优势菌种（如黑色素瘤中Faecalibacterium，HCC中Akkermansia/Ruminococcaceae，NSCLC中Akkermansia/Alistipes）。\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s033\",\"s267\",\"s023\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b7b952d0d492ff2d26e93bff\",\"source_handle\":\"P0273\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"该综述仅纳入临床研究，排除了动物实验，因此其关于机制的解释（如T细胞激活）主要基于人类临床样本的相关性或FMT后的表型变化，而非直接的分子通路解析。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s033\",\"s267\",\"s023\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::b81452e6f8c2cf88f589c219\",\"source_handle\":\"P0273\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"发现的菌群与疗效的关联多为观察性结果，存在混杂因素（如饮食、生活方式、合并用药），不能直接视为因果证据，除非有FMT等干预性研究的支持。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s033\",\"s267\",\"s023\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::17045e9a74e743196a9ec5a9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0273\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"不同研究间使用的测序区域（V3-V4, V4, V4-V5）和分析方法不同，导致具体菌种鉴定可能存在偏差，比较时需考虑技术异质性。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s033\",\"s267\",\"s023\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::91f185a2d063fd5c2d47e7ba\",\"source_handle\":\"P0273\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"FMT研究样本量极小（n=10, n=15），结果仅代表初步安全性和可行性，不能代表普遍疗效。\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s033\",\"s267\",\"s023\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::7acb9f11d1a63262fa2e4e18\",\"source_handle\":\"P0273\",\"field_path\":[\"supplement_materials\"],\"value\":[{\"auxiliary_material\":\"The review details methodological heterogeneity across the included studies, such as variations in sequencing regions (V3-V4, V4, V4-V5), sample collection times, and cancer types, which complicates direct comparison. It also notes that only two studies examined gastrointestinal toxicity (colitis), finding low Bacteroidetes abundance associated with higher risk. The authors mention that while FMT response rates in these small studies are comparable to RCTs for Clostridioides difficile infection, the cancer FMT studies themselves are described as 'breakthrough clinical studies' rather than large-scale Phase III trials. The review excludes animal models to focus on clinical applicability but acknowledges that most included studies are observational (retrospective or prospective cohorts) rather than randomized interventions.\",\"evidence\":[],\"gap_id\":\"phase_iii_rct_evidence\",\"judgment_path\":\"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\level2\\\\external\\\\N48436b3aa73aea86f35f-f45b87be8e30256e\\\\round_1\\\\supplements\\\\phase_iii_rct_evidence\\\\attempt-c7j_i2fn\\\\source_units\\\\SU03_search_candidate_2d56a11919\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\"limitations\":[],\"material_ready\":true,\"material_usefulness\":\"supporting\",\"outline_action\":\"Use this material to characterize the current evidence landscape as primarily observational with emerging but limited interventional data. Cite the authors' explicit statement that well-designed RCTs are still required to establish causality and clinical guidelines. Use the details of the Baruch and Davar studies to illustrate the proof-of-concept stage of FMT in oncology, contrasting their small sample sizes and specific indication (refractory melanoma) against the gap's requirement for large-scale Phase III trials in solid tumors. This supports the conclusion that the gap remains unresolved due to the immaturity of interventional trial data.\",\"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"remaining_gap\":\"The specific evidence requested—completed large-scale randomized controlled Phase III clinical trials confirming microbiome intervention (FMT) efficacy in ICI-treated solid tumors—is not present in this material. The available FMT data is limited to small-sample (n=10, n=15), early-phase studies restricted to refractory melanoma, not broad solid tumors. The authors' call for future robust RCTs and multicentre trials indicates that such Phase III evidence does not yet exist or was not captured in this review (search up to March 2021).\",\"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\":false,\"status\":\"unmet\",\"useful_material\":\"This study is a clinical review analyzing 10 studies (total n=467 patients) regarding the gut microbiome and immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) outcomes in solid tumors (melanoma, HCC, NSCLC, RCC). It reports that baseline microbiome diversity and composition (e.g., enrichment of Faecalibacterium, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) are associated with improved progression-free survival (PFS) and overall survival (OS), while Bacteroidales abundance often correlates with non-response. Crucially for the gap, the authors highlight two FMT clinical studies (Baruch et al., n=10; Davar et al., n=15) in anti-PD-1 refractory metastatic melanoma. These studies demonstrated safety and potential efficacy (30-40% response rate) when combining FMT from responders with ICI re-challenge. However, the authors explicitly state that 'further well-designed RCTs are required to explore the causal effects' and that 'future international multicentre trials will be required to provide comprehensive and reliable data.' They note that up-to-date practice guidelines based on clinical evidence are not yet available.\"}],\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s033\",\"s023\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5f4a3067c60d9ca5815c45e7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0273\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"known_gaps\":[{\"asset_id\":\"asset-b5c2e925a4132b88eff6\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-7f937d5566b4c12030ce\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-a96686bee2f7be7a8dd8\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-724817b1ad2fa81c8182\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-ba354d40740f64366cbf\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"},{\"asset_id\":\"asset-403bce67afb0fdb07c1f\",\"kind\":\"asset\",\"reason\":\"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\"status\":\"caption_only\"}],\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s033\",\"s267\",\"s023\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9c0275a5e34adb0279612f6a\",\"source_handle\":\"P0273\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s267\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::18f1e0027dc274d710422af9\",\"source_handle\":\"P0303\",\"field_path\":[\"material_depth\"],\"value\":\"fulltext\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s128\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::472b4940b21448ebf2b32460\",\"source_handle\":\"P0303\",\"field_path\":[\"material_status\"],\"value\":\"resolved\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s128\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a11c34c0060b848051885d47\",\"source_handle\":\"P0303\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"approach\"],\"value\":\"As a narrative review, the authors systematically organized existing literature into thematic sections: (1) mechanisms of anti-tumor immunity and ICI resistance; (2) biological crosstalk between gut microbiota and the immune system; (3) summary of clinical studies correlating microbiome composition with ICI response in specific cancers; (4) evaluation of microbiome modulation strategies (diet, probiotics, FMT); and (5) discussion of methodological limitations and future directions. The approach involves synthesizing findings from preclinical models and human clinical trials, comparing results across different studies, and critically assessing the consistency and reliability of reported microbial associations.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s128\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c2f9240e3395358f5801fe35\",\"source_handle\":\"P0303\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"Provides a structured synthesis of the complex relationship between gut microbiota and ICI efficacy, categorizing mechanisms (metabolite-mediated, immune modulation) and summarizing clinical correlations across multiple tumor types.\",\"limits\":\"As a narrative review, it does not perform a systematic meta-analysis with statistical pooling. The field is characterized by high heterogeneity and conflicting results, which the review acknowledges but cannot fully resolve due to the nature of the included studies.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s128\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::5de6adbf5a5bf3c90fe3d432\",\"source_handle\":\"P0303\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"contribution_and_limits\"],\"value\":{\"contribution\":\"Identifies critical methodological pitfalls in current microbiome research, such as sample handling inconsistencies, lack of strain-level resolution, and uncontrolled confounders (diet, antibiotics), offering a roadmap for improving future study design.\",\"limits\":\"The recommendations for future research are prospective; the review itself relies on existing data which may be biased by publication or selection effects common in early-stage microbiome studies.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s128\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::c20c39cdfa67e57e360435e8\",\"source_handle\":\"P0303\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"In melanoma and NSCLC patients treated with ICIs\",\"finding\":\"Specific bacterial taxa are correlated with ICI response, but results are often conflicting. Generally, higher alpha-diversity and abundance of certain commensals like *Bifidobacterium*, *Faecalibacterium prausnitzii*, and *Akkermansia muciniphila* are associated with better responses and prolonged progression-free survival (PFS). Conversely, some studies link *Bacteroides* species to either positive or negative outcomes depending on the specific species and ICI type.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s128\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::d0fc4b4517bdbf1143ec35ec\",\"source_handle\":\"P0303\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Preclinical and mechanistic studies\",\"finding\":\"Gut microbiota modulate immunity via metabolites (e.g., short-chain fatty acids, inosine) and surface molecules (e.g., LPS, PSA). For instance, *B. pseudolongum* produces inosine which enhances T-cell activation via A2AR signaling, and *A. muciniphila* can induce pro-inflammatory cytokines and suppress Tregs, thereby enhancing anti-tumor immunity.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s128\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ec736986f0c0de06668a4018\",\"source_handle\":\"P0303\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"key_findings\"],\"value\":{\"conditions\":\"Clinical intervention studies\",\"finding\":\"Fecal Microbiota Transplantation (FMT) from responders to non-responders has shown promise in augmenting ICI efficacy in subsets of melanoma patients. Dietary interventions rich in fiber and probiotic supplementation are being investigated in ongoing trials to improve outcomes.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s128\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::555e4db4924ab38f3df0dcd7\",\"source_handle\":\"P0303\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"paper_kind\"],\"value\":\"review\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s128\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::df86d43f8b68022fc8065f20\",\"source_handle\":\"P0303\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"problem_or_question\"],\"value\":\"The review addresses the problem that a significant proportion of patients with solid tumors exhibit primary or acquired resistance to ICIs. It seeks to understand the role of the gut microbiome in this resistance and response variability, aiming to identify microbial signatures associated with therapeutic success and adverse events, and to evaluate potential microbiome-based interventions to improve clinical outcomes.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s128\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a84c70da599a192104b09297\",\"source_handle\":\"P0303\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"research_scope\"],\"value\":\"The review focuses on the interaction between the gut microbiome and the host immune system, specifically in the context of cancer immunotherapy using Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors (ICIs). It covers preclinical mechanisms and clinical observations across various solid tumors, primarily melanoma and non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC), while also addressing methodological challenges and future interventional strategies.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s128\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::671f0dd98d7293b1c5de958f\",\"source_handle\":\"P0303\",\"field_path\":[\"study_summary_A\",\"work_summary\"],\"value\":\"This article is a comprehensive review that synthesizes current knowledge on how the gut microbiota influences the efficacy and toxicity of cancer immunotherapy. It begins by outlining the biological basis of anti-tumor immunity and ICI resistance, then details the crosstalk between gut microbes and the immune system through metabolites and surface molecules. The core of the paper summarizes clinical evidence linking specific microbial signatures to ICI response in melanoma and lung cancer, highlighting both consistent trends and conflicting data. Finally, it discusses strategies for manipulating the microbiome (diet, probiotics, FMT) and identifies critical pitfalls in current research, such as heterogeneity, sampling issues, and lack of standardized protocols, proposing multi-omic approaches and rigorous trial designs for future studies.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s128\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::0f858b58e7a84b232efcd43e\",\"source_handle\":\"P0303\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"planning_summary\"],\"value\":\"This review serves as a foundational resource for understanding the mechanistic links and clinical correlations between gut microbiota and ICI efficacy in solid tumors. It provides a curated list of specific bacterial taxa and metabolites associated with response/resistance, outlines the biological pathways involved (e.g., T-cell activation, Treg suppression), and highlights the current state of interventional strategies (FMT, diet, probiotics). It is particularly useful for establishing the 'mechanism' facet and identifying key variables for the 'efficacy' facet, while also providing critical context on the limitations and heterogeneity of current evidence.\",\"role\":\"planner_interpretation\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s128\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::ff636bb09c91900788dba364\",\"source_handle\":\"P0303\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"The associations are largely correlative and vary by cancer type and ICI class. The review explicitly notes conflicts in the literature regarding specific taxa (e.g., *Bacteroides*), so these should not be taken as universal rules without considering study-specific contexts.\",\"contribution\":\"Summarizes clinical evidence linking specific microbial signatures to ICI response in solid tumors. It lists taxa associated with improved outcomes (e.g., *Bifidobacterium*, *Faecalibacterium*, *Akkermansia*) and those linked to resistance or conflicting results (e.g., certain *Bacteroides* species). It also notes the general association between higher alpha-diversity and better response.\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s128\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6362a792e1c5e373bfb230dc\",\"source_handle\":\"P0303\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"Many mechanistic insights are derived from preclinical mouse models (e.g., germ-free mice, syngeneic tumor models). While plausible, direct translation to human physiology requires caution. The review distinguishes between preclinical evidence and clinical observations.\",\"contribution\":\"Details the biological mechanisms by which gut microbiota influence anti-tumor immunity. Key mechanisms include: (1) Metabolite production (e.g., inosine from *B. pseudolongum* activating A2AR signaling to enhance T-cell function; SCFAs influencing DC maturation and Treg polarization); (2) Surface molecule interactions (e.g., LPS triggering TLRs; PSA modulating Tregs); (3) Modulation of the tumor microenvironment (TME) via induction of pro-inflammatory cytokines (IFN-gamma, IL-12) and suppression of immunosuppressive cells (Tregs, MDSCs).\",\"facet_id\":\"F2\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s128\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::32e62e3e492f85b841f96004\",\"source_handle\":\"P0303\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"facet_contributions\"],\"value\":{\"boundaries\":\"Most interventional data are from small-scale studies or ongoing trials. Long-term safety and efficacy of FMT and probiotics in cancer patients are not yet fully established. The review emphasizes the need for larger, randomized controlled trials.\",\"contribution\":\"Evaluates the potential of microbiome manipulation strategies (diet, probiotics, FMT, BCT) to enhance ICI efficacy. It reviews ongoing clinical trials and preliminary results, such as FMT from responders improving outcomes in melanoma patients.\",\"facet_id\":\"F1\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s128\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::de2428812c6d732ea74cd0c2\",\"source_handle\":\"P0303\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"Discussion of methodological pitfalls including sample handling, lack of standardization, confounding factors (diet, antibiotics, demographics), and the difference between stool and tissue microbiota.\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s128\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::9c07444f0c3ecf2b3eea4f55\",\"source_handle\":\"P0303\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"broader_review_uses\"],\"value\":{\"material\":\"Overview of the cancer immunity cycle and ICI resistance mechanisms (host-related, tumor-intrinsic, environmental).\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s128\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::70f572b3471b6818dfa56246\",\"source_handle\":\"P0303\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"The review covers multiple solid tumor types, but most detailed clinical data are for melanoma and NSCLC. Findings may not generalize to all solid tumors.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s128\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::6987372e152f4c3d942f37c6\",\"source_handle\":\"P0303\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"Conflicting results for certain bacterial genera (e.g., *Bacteroides*) are highlighted; do not assume a single direction of effect without specifying the context (species, ICI type, patient cohort).\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s128\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::a68b80285f0c187259d974ee\",\"source_handle\":\"P0303\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"Mechanistic insights are often based on preclinical models; distinguish between proven human mechanisms and hypothesized pathways supported by animal data.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s128\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::2a9a907e359900629c7dc170\",\"source_handle\":\"P0303\",\"field_path\":[\"review_planning_B\",\"scope_interpretation_cautions\"],\"value\":\"Interventional strategies (FMT, probiotics) are largely investigational; avoid presenting them as standard of care.\",\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s128\"]},{\"atom_id\":\"atom::83a8637ae312a5f8bb50d396\",\"source_handle\":\"P0303\",\"field_path\":[\"card_material\"],\"value\":{\"material_scope\":\"fulltext\"},\"role\":\"evidence\",\"snapshot_ids\":[\"s128\"]}],\"snapshot_index\":{\"s058\":\"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\"s234\":\"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\"s149\":\"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\"s255\":\"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\"s238\":\"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\",\"s157\":\"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\"s246\":\"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\",\"s008\":\"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\"s129\":\"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\",\"s199\":\"snapshot::aee91b6d254c74392754ffb3\",\"s203\":\"snapshot::b48b92078f04672f80082d00\",\"s046\":\"snapshot::33eb067b80204dcb68c3dbc6\",\"s072\":\"snapshot::4debf19bd260cc81e2d804ee\",\"s081\":\"snapshot::55488d84dbb359a3345c319f\",\"s132\":\"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\",\"s056\":\"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\"s061\":\"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\"s286\":\"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\"s214\":\"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\",\"s208\":\"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\",\"s060\":\"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\"s031\":\"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\"s160\":\"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\"s074\":\"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\",\"s265\":\"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\"s251\":\"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\"s035\":\"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\",\"s010\":\"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\"s039\":\"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\",\"s030\":\"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\",\"s150\":\"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\",\"s041\":\"snapshot::2ebf71c6aa2b1657b267b130\",\"s017\":\"snapshot::153461ac1a5cb9b5a31c3121\",\"s263\":\"snapshot::e83de03b33da0c831779d170\",\"s144\":\"snapshot::82bffb4d0f097201933ac437\",\"s198\":\"snapshot::ae6fc092083bad76a3be286e\",\"s154\":\"snapshot::890fce072a8f724aaec9108f\",\"s278\":\"snapshot::f63dfcb79a3ed06be7080d88\",\"s130\":\"snapshot::791f861f7c03887eb2ba1797\",\"s029\":\"snapshot::20309b87fd0e8cfe50d8893d\",\"s187\":\"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\"s107\":\"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\",\"s120\":\"snapshot::73efa1be4be250cf312dbe78\",\"s036\":\"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\"s202\":\"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\",\"s228\":\"snapshot::c96dcd391e3ff6d5952be10a\",\"s268\":\"snapshot::eb5aa52fd3ffd49fe0ad1176\",\"s123\":\"snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b\",\"s227\":\"snapshot::c7c67d13abcc3ba3a71d2af4\",\"s018\":\"snapshot::153738efad1ff78582447def\",\"s065\":\"snapshot::44b1f3bad783421ccdb817ed\",\"s195\":\"snapshot::ab105c805d6f74d4e02b550b\",\"s117\":\"snapshot::7370217b0d1083d4f465a9fd\",\"s209\":\"snapshot::b8f4ede79d64928928c3569c\",\"s241\":\"snapshot::d1590c0e09f64bdeb0f7b69b\",\"s201\":\"snapshot::b027266378a52b2c51ee323b\",\"s272\":\"snapshot::ee1ea13dd08d157b2c4c0b78\",\"s220\":\"snapshot::c1380d633739b6409c09a4c3\",\"s027\":\"snapshot::1fd227bf27d6d15554f9ced9\",\"s088\":\"snapshot::5b707a9c2a4912437225849f\",\"s204\":\"snapshot::b4fe98bf4129f2a01928c2de\",\"s069\":\"snapshot::49f12e61cfb8da920f6cf528\",\"s071\":\"snapshot::4c223c48c000f6845789e3b9\",\"s047\":\"snapshot::34a888801e8e6d821b264263\",\"s101\":\"snapshot::668c479a5777d8a189e172af\",\"s135\":\"snapshot::7f4d4d07befb7d6373432503\",\"s025\":\"snapshot::1e84d153ee9b84bcfe58dd94\",\"s109\":\"snapshot::6e75af540e1165fa53a1929a\",\"s033\":\"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\"s023\":\"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\",\"s267\":\"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\"s128\":\"snapshot::77186f2ef181ee4ddaa8ebfc\"},\"tool_materials\":[{\"tool_id\":\"tool::08347994f232faa9bf00712d0fc5c3c3b5c2a68fb2b93f49d6b45df576b6f1b9\",\"value\":{\"need_id\":\"N61bd5cdf82bc1980ec2a-fe99d495492aaf34\",\"question\":\"是否有已完成的大型随机对照 III 期临床试验证实微生物干预（如 FMT）在 ICI 治疗实体瘤中的疗效？\",\"intended_use\":\"application_outcome\",\"decision\":\"provider_retry\",\"usable_content\":\"现有数据与用户询问的“已完成大型随机对照 III 期临床试验”设置不一致，提供的证据主要为 I/II 期研究，且研究设计（RCT vs 单臂）与人群（初治 vs 经治）存在差异。TACITO 试验（Phase 2a RCT）中，d-FMT 组相较于 p-FMT 组在 12 个月 PFS 率、中位 PFS 及中位 OS 上数值更高，提示正向差异，但原文未提供统计检验结果，不能认定具有统计学显著性。单臂试验结果方向不一致：ICI 经治人群（MITRIC 试验）ORR 为 0%，提示负向或无疗效；而初治黑色素瘤（MIMic 试验）或 NSCLC/黑色素瘤（FMT-LUMINate 试验）ORR 介于 65%-80%，提示正向差异。这表明微生物干预疗效可能受治疗线数影响，但缺乏 III 期 RCT 证实。\\n\\n适用条件：仅基于提供的 I/II 期试验数据；数值差异不代表统计显著；不包含用户指定的 III 期 RCT 证据；不推断未报告的机制。\\nTACITO trial (P0593) / 12-month PFS rate / Phase 2a RCT, mRCC, first-line：d-FMT: 70%；p-FMT: 41%\\nTACITO trial (P0593) / Median PFS / Phase 2a RCT, mRCC, first-line：d-FMT: 24.0 months；p-FMT: 9.0 months\\nTACITO trial (P0593) / Median OS / Phase 2a RCT, mRCC, first-line：d-FMT: 41.0 months；p-FMT: 28.3 months\\nMITRIC trial (P0578) / ORR / Phase IIa single-arm, ICI-refractory：All patients (n=12): 0%\\nMITRIC trial (P0578) / Median PFS / Phase IIa single-arm, ICI-refractory：All patients (n=12): 1.5 months\\nMIMic trial (P0577) / ORR / Phase I single-arm, first-line melanoma：All patients (n=20): 65%\\nMIMic trial (P0577) / Median PFS / Phase I single-arm, first-line melanoma：All patients (n=20): 29.6 months\\nFMT-LUMINate (P0583) / ORR / Phase 2 single-arm, NSCLC：NSCLC cohort: 80%\\nFMT-LUMINate (P0583) / ORR / Phase 2 single-arm, Melanoma：Melanoma cohort: 75%\",\"conditions\":[\"TACITO trial (P0593)\",\"Phase 2a RCT, mRCC, first-line\",\"MITRIC trial (P0578)\",\"Phase IIa single-arm, ICI-refractory\",\"MIMic trial (P0577)\",\"Phase I single-arm, first-line melanoma\",\"FMT-LUMINate (P0583)\",\"Phase 2 single-arm, NSCLC\",\"Phase 2 single-arm, Melanoma\"],\"limits\":[\"已完成并发表主要结局数据的 Phase III RCT 研究（如注册号为 NCT 开头的 III 期试验结果）。\"],\"still_missing\":\"已完成并发表主要结局数据的 Phase III RCT 研究（如注册号为 NCT 开头的 III 期试验结果）。\",\"allowed_use\":[\"background_context\",\"explicit_objectives\",\"explicit_method_summaries\",\"explicit_reported_findings\",\"explicit_leads\"],\"sources\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0578\",\"paper_id\":\"d9577b3a29bd8aec60c9e27c6a56a63faf3f4a27\",\"title\":\"Safety and efficacy of fecal microbiota transplantation in solid cancers resistant to immune checkpoint inhibitors: results of the MITRIC trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1136/jitc-2026-015122\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0578\",\"paper_id\":\"d9577b3a29bd8aec60c9e27c6a56a63faf3f4a27\",\"title\":\"Safety and efficacy of fecal microbiota transplantation in solid cancers resistant to immune checkpoint inhibitors: results of the MITRIC trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1136/jitc-2026-015122\"},{\"paper_id\":\"69b4c5f84be199181be6ab5d3124f306462234f3\",\"title\":\"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus pembrolizumab and axitinib in metastatic renal cell carcinoma: the randomized phase 2 TACITO trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41591-025-04189-2\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"paper_id\":\"69b4c5f84be199181be6ab5d3124f306462234f3\",\"title\":\"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus pembrolizumab and axitinib in metastatic renal cell carcinoma: the randomized phase 2 TACITO trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41591-025-04189-2\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"paper_id\":\"a1c056e6d54a3498db16737d087fae44f686a900\",\"title\":\"Fecal microbiota transplantation improves anti-PD-1 inhibitor efficacy in unresectable or metastatic solid cancers refractory to anti-PD-1 inhibitor.\",\"year\":\"2024\",\"doi\":\"10.1016/j.chom.2024.06.010\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0594\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0577\",\"paper_id\":\"20c143d5373eab0bfea2067cf66b0e260dfeb1ef\",\"title\":\"Improved survival in advanced melanoma patients treated with fecal microbiota transplantation using healthy donor stool in combination with anti-PD1: final results of the MIMic phase 1 trial\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1136/jitc-2025-012659\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0583\",\"paper_id\":\"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\"title\":\"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:290154100\",\"title\":\"Navigating the gut–metabolite–immune axis: enhancing efficacy and mitigating toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.3389/fimmu.2026.1803970\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0584\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_identity\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0577\",\"paper_id\":\"20c143d5373eab0bfea2067cf66b0e260dfeb1ef\",\"title\":\"Improved survival in advanced melanoma patients treated with fecal microbiota transplantation using healthy donor stool in combination with anti-PD1: final results of the MIMic phase 1 trial\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1136/jitc-2025-012659\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0577\",\"paper_id\":\"20c143d5373eab0bfea2067cf66b0e260dfeb1ef\",\"title\":\"Improved survival in advanced melanoma patients treated with fecal microbiota transplantation using healthy donor stool in combination with anti-PD1: final results of the MIMic phase 1 trial\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1136/jitc-2025-012659\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0577\",\"paper_id\":\"20c143d5373eab0bfea2067cf66b0e260dfeb1ef\",\"title\":\"Improved survival in advanced melanoma patients treated with fecal microbiota transplantation using healthy donor stool in combination with anti-PD1: final results of the MIMic phase 1 trial\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1136/jitc-2025-012659\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0577\",\"paper_id\":\"20c143d5373eab0bfea2067cf66b0e260dfeb1ef\",\"title\":\"Improved survival in advanced melanoma patients treated with fecal microbiota transplantation using healthy donor stool in combination with anti-PD1: final results of the MIMic phase 1 trial\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1136/jitc-2025-012659\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0578\",\"paper_id\":\"d9577b3a29bd8aec60c9e27c6a56a63faf3f4a27\",\"title\":\"Safety and efficacy of fecal microbiota transplantation in solid cancers resistant to immune checkpoint inhibitors: results of the MITRIC trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1136/jitc-2026-015122\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0578\",\"paper_id\":\"d9577b3a29bd8aec60c9e27c6a56a63faf3f4a27\",\"title\":\"Safety and efficacy of fecal microbiota transplantation in solid cancers resistant to immune checkpoint inhibitors: results of the MITRIC trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1136/jitc-2026-015122\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0578\",\"paper_id\":\"d9577b3a29bd8aec60c9e27c6a56a63faf3f4a27\",\"title\":\"Safety and efficacy of fecal microbiota transplantation in solid cancers resistant to immune checkpoint inhibitors: results of the MITRIC trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1136/jitc-2026-015122\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0583\",\"paper_id\":\"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\"title\":\"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\"}],\"provenance\":{\"downloads\":0,\"model_calls\":0,\"source\":\"judge\",\"whole_paper_rereads\":0},\"chapter_ids\":[\"Ch5\"],\"unit_key\":\"\"}},{\"tool_id\":\"tool::7ba17796c4c79773a841d526a22cf63e3dd49f281a311dbd209fd1524017ba51\",\"value\":{\"need_id\":\"N48436b3aa73aea86f35f-b3c8ffc2a0ced9d8\",\"question\":\"是否有已完成的大型随机对照 III 期临床试验证实微生物干预（如 FMT）在 ICI 治疗实体瘤中的疗效？\",\"intended_use\":\"mechanism\",\"decision\":\"answer_from_local\",\"usable_content\":\"现有文献中尚未发现已完成的大型随机对照 III 期临床试验证实微生物干预（如 FMT）在实体瘤中的疗效。目前最高级别的证据来自 Phase IIa 阶段的随机对照试验和单臂研究，结果呈现异质性且未达成最终确证。\\n\\n具体而言，TACITO 试验是一项针对转移性肾细胞癌（mRCC）一线治疗患者的 Phase 2a 随机双盲安慰剂对照试验。虽然其次要终点中位无进展生存期（PFS）显著延长（24.0个月 vs 9.0个月，HR=0.50, P=0.035），但主要终点 12 个月 PFS 率未达到统计学显著差异（70% vs 41%, P=0.053），且总生存期（OS）虽呈有利趋势但未达显著性（P=0.167）。这表明在特定癌种和一线治疗背景下，FMT 显示出潜在的临床活性信号，但尚不足以作为确证性证据。\\n\\n相比之下，MITRIC 试验是一项针对多种晚期实体瘤（包括黑色素瘤、头颈鳞癌等）ICI 耐药患者的单臂 Phase IIa 篮式试验。该研究结果显示 FMT 安全性良好，但临床疗效有限：客观缓解率（ORR）为 0%，中位 PFS 仅为 1.5 个月，仅 1 名患者获得长期疾病稳定。机制分析提示，这种疗效局限可能与供体菌群定植短暂、宿主基线免疫环境（如髓系优势、高 IL-8）反映的是疾病状态而非 FMT 的直接作用有关。\\n\\n此外，Kim 等人（2024）发表的一项前瞻性单臂研究显示，在抗 PD-1 耐药的晚期实体瘤中，FMT 联合抗 PD-1 治疗可获得 7.7% 的 ORR 和 46.2% 的疾病控制率，并鉴定出特定的有益菌株（Prevotella merdae Immunoactis）。然而，由于缺乏随机对照设计和较大的样本量，这属于概念验证性质的探索性数据。\\n\\n综上所述，尽管有 Phase 2a RCT 显示部分指标改善，也有单臂研究提供机制支持，但目前缺乏大型 III 期 RCT 来确证 FMT 在广泛实体瘤人群中的确切疗效和生存获益。现有的阴性或混合结果提示疗效高度依赖于癌症类型、治疗线数（一线 vs 耐药）、供体选择及宿主免疫背景。\\nMITRIC trial (P0578) / ORR: 0%; Median PFS: 1.5 months; Clinical benefit (SD >6mo): 1/12 patients / Phase IIa single-arm basket trial, ICI-refractory advanced solid tumors (melanoma, HNSCC, RCC, MSI-H pancreatic cancer)：Total (n=12): ORR 0%, Median PFS 1.5 mo\\nTACITO trial (P0593) / 12-month PFS rate: 70% vs 41% (P=0.053); Median PFS: 24.0 vs 9.0 months (HR=0.50, P=0.035); Median OS: 41.0 vs 28.3 months (P=0.167) / Phase 2a randomized double-blind placebo-controlled trial, treatment-naive metastatic RCC (pembrolizumab + axitinib)：Donor FMT (d-FMT) (n=23 approx based on total 45): 12-mo PFS 70%, Median PFS 24.0 mo, Median OS 41.0 mo；Placebo FMT (p-FMT) (n=22 approx based on total 45): 12-mo PFS 41%, Median PFS 9.0 mo, Median OS 28.3 mo\\nKim et al. (P0594) / ORR: 7.7%; DCR: 46.2% / Prospective single-arm single-center study, anti-PD-1 refractory advanced solid cancers (gastric, esophageal, HCC)：Total (n=13): ORR 7.7%, DCR 46.2%\\n\\n截至当前材料覆盖的时间范围（主要文献发表于2024-2025年，系统综述更新至2026年中），尚无已完成的、大规模随机对照 III 期临床试验证实微生物干预（如 FMT）在 ICI 治疗实体瘤中的确切疗效。现有最高级别的临床证据为 II 期随机对照试验（RCT）。例如，TACITO 试验是一项针对转移性肾细胞癌（mRCC）患者的双盲、安慰剂对照 Phase 2a RCT，结果显示虽然中位无进展生存期（PFS）显著延长（24.0个月 vs 9.0个月，HR=0.50, P=0.035），但主要终点（12个月 PFS 率）未达到统计学显著性（70% vs 41%, P=0.053），且总生存期（OS）未显示显著差异。此外，多项单臂 II 期研究（如 MITRIC 试验在 ICI 耐药患者中 ORR 为 0%，FMT-LUMINate 试验在黑色素瘤中 ORR 为 70% 但伴随高比例严重免疫相关不良事件）提供了初步信号，但缺乏对照组验证。多篇综述明确指出，目前证据主要来自回顾性队列或早期（I/II 期）试验，亟需大规模、多中心、标准化的 III 期 RCT 来确证疗效并建立预测模型。\\n\\n[\\\"This study is a systematic review and meta-analysis (search up to September 30, 2024) that included 10 studies involving 164 patients with solid tumors treated with FMT combined with ICIs. The authors report that the included studies comprised 5 phase I trials, 4 phase II–III trials, and 3 randomized controlled trials (RCTs), but note that most were early-phase clinical trials with small sample sizes. The pooled objective response rate (ORR) was 43%, with subgroup analysis showing higher ORR (60%) for anti-PD-1 combined with anti-CTLA-4 therapy compared to monotherapy (37%). Crucially, the authors conclude in both the Abstract and Discussion that 'larger-scale randomized controlled trials with long-term follow-up are required to confirm and optimize treatment protocols' and highlight the 'absence of randomized controlled trials' (referring to large-scale/definitive ones) as a limitation. This material directly addresses the gap question by confirming that while preliminary RCT data exists, completed large-scale Phase III evidence is currently lacking and identified as a necessary future step.\\\", \\\"This review explicitly addresses the current clinical evidence level for microbiome interventions in cancer immunotherapy. The authors report that for Fecal Microbiota Transplantation (FMT), the most developed clinical evidence comes from Phase 1 studies in melanoma patients showing recovery of anti–PD-1 response in some cases. For colorectal cancer (CRC), the authors cite a Phase 2 study evaluating FMT with immunotherapy and targeted therapy that reported improvement signals but was designed without a control group, making effectiveness determination difficult. The authors conclude that large-scale prospective studies and well-designed randomized controlled trials are still needed before routine clinical use, and frame FMT in CRC as an investigational intervention rather than an established treatment.\\\", \\\"This study is a clinical review analyzing 10 studies (total n=467 patients) regarding the gut microbiome and immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) outcomes in solid tumors (melanoma, HCC, NSCLC, RCC). It reports that baseline microbiome diversity and composition (e.g., enrichment of Faecalibacterium, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) are associated with improved progression-free survival (PFS) and overall survival (OS), while Bacteroidales abundance often correlates with non-response. Crucially for the gap, the authors highlight two FMT clinical studies (Baruch et al., n=10; Davar et al., n=15) in anti-PD-1 refractory metastatic melanoma. These studies demonstrated safety and potential efficacy (30-40% response rate) when combining FMT from responders with ICI re-challenge. However, the authors explicitly state that 'further well-designed RCTs are required to explore the causal effects' and that 'future international multicentre trials will be required to provide comprehensive and reliable data.' They note that up-to-date practice guidelines based on clinical evidence are not yet available.\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"The study provides detailed safety data (42% grade 1–2 adverse events, 37% grade 3–4 adverse events) and mechanistic hypotheses (e.g., increasing beneficial bacteria like Akkermansia muciniphila, modulating tumor microenvironment) which, while not validating the Phase III gap, offer context on why such trials are being pursued. It also notes heterogeneity in FMT protocols (donor sources, administration routes) as a barrier that large-scale trials need to standardize.\\\", \\\"The review details mechanistic pathways linking specific gut microbes to immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) response, which provides biological rationale for ongoing trials. For example, Fusobacterium nucleatum (Fn) is described as promoting immune evasion via Fap2-TIGIT binding and chemotherapy resistance, while Peptostreptococcus anaerobius (Pa) is linked to anti–PD-1 resistance via MDSC activation. Conversely, beneficial bacteria like Bifidobacterium are noted in preclinical models to enhance antitumor efficacy of PD-1 blockade. The authors also discuss confounding factors in microbiome research (e.g., stool transit time, BMI) that complicate biomarker and intervention standardization, relevant for designing future rigorous trials.\\\", \\\"The review details methodological heterogeneity across the included studies, such as variations in sequencing regions (V3-V4, V4, V4-V5), sample collection times, and cancer types, which complicates direct comparison. It also notes that only two studies examined gastrointestinal toxicity (colitis), finding low Bacteroidetes abundance associated with higher risk. The authors mention that while FMT response rates in these small studies are comparable to RCTs for Clostridioides difficile infection, the cancer FMT studies themselves are described as 'breakthrough clinical studies' rather than large-scale Phase III trials. The review excludes animal models to focus on clinical applicability but acknowledges that most included studies are observational (retrospective or prospective cohorts) rather than randomized interventions.\\\"]\\n\\n现有材料未提供已完成的大型随机对照 III 期临床试验证实微生物干预（如 FMT）在 ICI 治疗实体瘤中的疗效。相反，多项研究明确指出该领域仍处于早期阶段：MITRIC 试验是一项单臂 IIa 期篮子试验，结果显示在 ICI 难治性晚期癌症患者中 FMT 无客观缓解（ORR 0%），仅个别患者获得临床获益；TACITO 试验虽为随机双盲安慰剂对照试验，但仅为 IIa 期，且主要终点（12个月无进展生存率）未达到统计学显著差异（70% vs 41%, P=0.053），尽管次要终点中位 PFS 有显著改善（24.0 vs 9.0 个月, P=0.035）。此外，一项涵盖 10 项研究（164 名患者）的系统综述与荟萃分析指出，目前证据主要来自早期 Phase I/II 试验和小样本 RCT，作者明确强调“缺乏大型随机对照试验”，并呼吁进行大规模、多中心的 III 期 RCT 以确认疗效和优化方案。因此，截至这些来源的时间点，尚无完成的 III 期 RCT 确证其疗效，这一证据缺口被反复提及为当前研究的局限性及未来方向。\\n\\n现有材料未提供已完成的大型随机对照 III 期临床试验证实微生物干预（如 FMT）在 ICI 治疗实体瘤中的疗效。相反，多项研究明确指出该领域仍处于早期阶段：MITRIC 试验是一项单臂 IIa 期篮子试验，结果显示在 ICI 难治性晚期癌症患者中 FMT 无客观缓解（ORR 0%），仅个别患者获得临床获益；TACITO 试验虽为随机双盲安慰剂对照试验，但仅为 IIa 期，且主要终点（12个月无进展生存率）未达到统计学显著差异（70% vs 41%, P=0.053），尽管次要终点中位 PFS 有显著改善（24.0 vs 9.0 个月, P=0.035）。此外，一项涵盖 10 项研究（164 名患者）的系统综述与荟萃分析指出，目前证据主要来自早期 Phase I/II 试验和小样本 RCT，作者明确强调“缺乏大型随机对照试验”，并呼吁进行大规模、多中心的 III 期 RCT 以确认疗效和优化方案。因此，截至这些来源的时间点，尚无完成的 III 期 RCT 确证其疗效，这一证据缺口被反复提及为当前研究的局限性及未来方向。\",\"conditions\":[],\"limits\":[],\"still_missing\":\"\",\"allowed_use\":[\"background_context\",\"explicit_objectives\",\"explicit_method_summaries\",\"explicit_reported_findings\",\"explicit_leads\"],\"sources\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0578\",\"paper_id\":\"d9577b3a29bd8aec60c9e27c6a56a63faf3f4a27\",\"title\":\"Safety and efficacy of fecal microbiota transplantation in solid cancers resistant to immune checkpoint inhibitors: results of the MITRIC trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1136/jitc-2026-015122\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0578\",\"paper_id\":\"d9577b3a29bd8aec60c9e27c6a56a63faf3f4a27\",\"title\":\"Safety and efficacy of fecal microbiota transplantation in solid cancers resistant to immune checkpoint inhibitors: results of the MITRIC trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1136/jitc-2026-015122\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0212\",\"paper_id\":\"5af3aee4ca5f3778325d44c8432c8b71b95ca531\",\"title\":\"Microbiota boost immunotherapy? A meta-analysis dives into fecal microbiota transplantation and immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1186/s12916-025-04183-y\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0212\",\"paper_id\":\"5af3aee4ca5f3778325d44c8432c8b71b95ca531\",\"title\":\"Microbiota boost immunotherapy? A meta-analysis dives into fecal microbiota transplantation and immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1186/s12916-025-04183-y\"},{\"paper_id\":\"69b4c5f84be199181be6ab5d3124f306462234f3\",\"title\":\"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus pembrolizumab and axitinib in metastatic renal cell carcinoma: the randomized phase 2 TACITO trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41591-025-04189-2\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"canonical_paper_id\":\"OpenAlex:W4411127845\",\"title\":\"Microbiota boost immunotherapy? A meta-analysis dives into fecal microbiota transplantation and immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1186/s12916-025-04183-y\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_identity\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0590\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:286044272\",\"canonical_paper_id\":\"CorpusId:286044272\",\"title\":\"Gut microbiome in colorectal cancer: recent advances and clinical implications\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.3393/ac.2026.00010.0001\"},{\"canonical_paper_id\":\"OpenAlex:W3203589616\",\"title\":\"The Gut Microbiome and Cancer Immunotherapy: Can We Use the Gut Microbiome as a Predictive Biomarker for Clinical Response in Cancer Immunotherapy?\",\"year\":\"2021\",\"doi\":\"10.3390/cancers13194824\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_identity\"}],\"provenance\":{\"downloads\":0,\"model_calls\":0,\"source\":\"judge\",\"whole_paper_rereads\":0},\"chapter_ids\":[\"Ch5\"],\"unit_key\":\"\"}},{\"tool_id\":\"tool::d246d1ed6e11b1457bb047c36d5eb58b84347aa7af7e7fbc930c7090c626f8c4\",\"value\":{\"need_id\":\"N48436b3aa73aea86f35f-128da42822ca7b8e\",\"question\":\"是否有已完成的大型随机对照 III 期临床试验证实微生物干预（如 FMT）在 ICI 治疗实体瘤中的疗效？\",\"intended_use\":\"mechanism\",\"decision\":\"answer_from_local\",\"usable_content\":\"现有文献中尚未发现已完成的大型随机对照 III 期临床试验证实微生物干预（如 FMT）在实体瘤中的疗效。目前最高级别的证据来自 Phase IIa 阶段的随机对照试验和单臂研究，结果呈现异质性且未达成最终确证。\\n\\n具体而言，TACITO 试验是一项针对转移性肾细胞癌（mRCC）一线治疗患者的 Phase 2a 随机双盲安慰剂对照试验。虽然其次要终点中位无进展生存期（PFS）显著延长（24.0个月 vs 9.0个月，HR=0.50, P=0.035），但主要终点 12 个月 PFS 率未达到统计学显著差异（70% vs 41%, P=0.053），且总生存期（OS）虽呈有利趋势但未达显著性（P=0.167）。这表明在特定癌种和一线治疗背景下，FMT 显示出潜在的临床活性信号，但尚不足以作为确证性证据。\\n\\n相比之下，MITRIC 试验是一项针对多种晚期实体瘤（包括黑色素瘤、头颈鳞癌等）ICI 耐药患者的单臂 Phase IIa 篮式试验。该研究结果显示 FMT 安全性良好，但临床疗效有限：客观缓解率（ORR）为 0%，中位 PFS 仅为 1.5 个月，仅 1 名患者获得长期疾病稳定。机制分析提示，这种疗效局限可能与供体菌群定植短暂、宿主基线免疫环境（如髓系优势、高 IL-8）反映的是疾病状态而非 FMT 的直接作用有关。\\n\\n此外，Kim 等人（2024）发表的一项前瞻性单臂研究显示，在抗 PD-1 耐药的晚期实体瘤中，FMT 联合抗 PD-1 治疗可获得 7.7% 的 ORR 和 46.2% 的疾病控制率，并鉴定出特定的有益菌株（Prevotella merdae Immunoactis）。然而，由于缺乏随机对照设计和较大的样本量，这属于概念验证性质的探索性数据。\\n\\n综上所述，尽管有 Phase 2a RCT 显示部分指标改善，也有单臂研究提供机制支持，但目前缺乏大型 III 期 RCT 来确证 FMT 在广泛实体瘤人群中的确切疗效和生存获益。现有的阴性或混合结果提示疗效高度依赖于癌症类型、治疗线数（一线 vs 耐药）、供体选择及宿主免疫背景。\\nMITRIC trial (P0578) / ORR: 0%; Median PFS: 1.5 months; Clinical benefit (SD >6mo): 1/12 patients / Phase IIa single-arm basket trial, ICI-refractory advanced solid tumors (melanoma, HNSCC, RCC, MSI-H pancreatic cancer)：Total (n=12): ORR 0%, Median PFS 1.5 mo\\nTACITO trial (P0593) / 12-month PFS rate: 70% vs 41% (P=0.053); Median PFS: 24.0 vs 9.0 months (HR=0.50, P=0.035); Median OS: 41.0 vs 28.3 months (P=0.167) / Phase 2a randomized double-blind placebo-controlled trial, treatment-naive metastatic RCC (pembrolizumab + axitinib)：Donor FMT (d-FMT) (n=23 approx based on total 45): 12-mo PFS 70%, Median PFS 24.0 mo, Median OS 41.0 mo；Placebo FMT (p-FMT) (n=22 approx based on total 45): 12-mo PFS 41%, Median PFS 9.0 mo, Median OS 28.3 mo\\nKim et al. (P0594) / ORR: 7.7%; DCR: 46.2% / Prospective single-arm single-center study, anti-PD-1 refractory advanced solid cancers (gastric, esophageal, HCC)：Total (n=13): ORR 7.7%, DCR 46.2%\\n\\n截至当前材料覆盖的时间范围（主要文献发表于2024-2025年，系统综述更新至2026年中），尚无已完成的、大规模随机对照 III 期临床试验证实微生物干预（如 FMT）在 ICI 治疗实体瘤中的确切疗效。现有最高级别的临床证据为 II 期随机对照试验（RCT）。例如，TACITO 试验是一项针对转移性肾细胞癌（mRCC）患者的双盲、安慰剂对照 Phase 2a RCT，结果显示虽然中位无进展生存期（PFS）显著延长（24.0个月 vs 9.0个月，HR=0.50, P=0.035），但主要终点（12个月 PFS 率）未达到统计学显著性（70% vs 41%, P=0.053），且总生存期（OS）未显示显著差异。此外，多项单臂 II 期研究（如 MITRIC 试验在 ICI 耐药患者中 ORR 为 0%，FMT-LUMINate 试验在黑色素瘤中 ORR 为 70% 但伴随高比例严重免疫相关不良事件）提供了初步信号，但缺乏对照组验证。多篇综述明确指出，目前证据主要来自回顾性队列或早期（I/II 期）试验，亟需大规模、多中心、标准化的 III 期 RCT 来确证疗效并建立预测模型。\\n\\n[\\\"This study is a systematic review and meta-analysis (search up to September 30, 2024) that included 10 studies involving 164 patients with solid tumors treated with FMT combined with ICIs. The authors report that the included studies comprised 5 phase I trials, 4 phase II–III trials, and 3 randomized controlled trials (RCTs), but note that most were early-phase clinical trials with small sample sizes. The pooled objective response rate (ORR) was 43%, with subgroup analysis showing higher ORR (60%) for anti-PD-1 combined with anti-CTLA-4 therapy compared to monotherapy (37%). Crucially, the authors conclude in both the Abstract and Discussion that 'larger-scale randomized controlled trials with long-term follow-up are required to confirm and optimize treatment protocols' and highlight the 'absence of randomized controlled trials' (referring to large-scale/definitive ones) as a limitation. This material directly addresses the gap question by confirming that while preliminary RCT data exists, completed large-scale Phase III evidence is currently lacking and identified as a necessary future step.\\\", \\\"This review explicitly addresses the current clinical evidence level for microbiome interventions in cancer immunotherapy. The authors report that for Fecal Microbiota Transplantation (FMT), the most developed clinical evidence comes from Phase 1 studies in melanoma patients showing recovery of anti–PD-1 response in some cases. For colorectal cancer (CRC), the authors cite a Phase 2 study evaluating FMT with immunotherapy and targeted therapy that reported improvement signals but was designed without a control group, making effectiveness determination difficult. The authors conclude that large-scale prospective studies and well-designed randomized controlled trials are still needed before routine clinical use, and frame FMT in CRC as an investigational intervention rather than an established treatment.\\\", \\\"This study is a clinical review analyzing 10 studies (total n=467 patients) regarding the gut microbiome and immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) outcomes in solid tumors (melanoma, HCC, NSCLC, RCC). It reports that baseline microbiome diversity and composition (e.g., enrichment of Faecalibacterium, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) are associated with improved progression-free survival (PFS) and overall survival (OS), while Bacteroidales abundance often correlates with non-response. Crucially for the gap, the authors highlight two FMT clinical studies (Baruch et al., n=10; Davar et al., n=15) in anti-PD-1 refractory metastatic melanoma. These studies demonstrated safety and potential efficacy (30-40% response rate) when combining FMT from responders with ICI re-challenge. However, the authors explicitly state that 'further well-designed RCTs are required to explore the causal effects' and that 'future international multicentre trials will be required to provide comprehensive and reliable data.' They note that up-to-date practice guidelines based on clinical evidence are not yet available.\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"The study provides detailed safety data (42% grade 1–2 adverse events, 37% grade 3–4 adverse events) and mechanistic hypotheses (e.g., increasing beneficial bacteria like Akkermansia muciniphila, modulating tumor microenvironment) which, while not validating the Phase III gap, offer context on why such trials are being pursued. It also notes heterogeneity in FMT protocols (donor sources, administration routes) as a barrier that large-scale trials need to standardize.\\\", \\\"The review details mechanistic pathways linking specific gut microbes to immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) response, which provides biological rationale for ongoing trials. For example, Fusobacterium nucleatum (Fn) is described as promoting immune evasion via Fap2-TIGIT binding and chemotherapy resistance, while Peptostreptococcus anaerobius (Pa) is linked to anti–PD-1 resistance via MDSC activation. Conversely, beneficial bacteria like Bifidobacterium are noted in preclinical models to enhance antitumor efficacy of PD-1 blockade. The authors also discuss confounding factors in microbiome research (e.g., stool transit time, BMI) that complicate biomarker and intervention standardization, relevant for designing future rigorous trials.\\\", \\\"The review details methodological heterogeneity across the included studies, such as variations in sequencing regions (V3-V4, V4, V4-V5), sample collection times, and cancer types, which complicates direct comparison. It also notes that only two studies examined gastrointestinal toxicity (colitis), finding low Bacteroidetes abundance associated with higher risk. The authors mention that while FMT response rates in these small studies are comparable to RCTs for Clostridioides difficile infection, the cancer FMT studies themselves are described as 'breakthrough clinical studies' rather than large-scale Phase III trials. The review excludes animal models to focus on clinical applicability but acknowledges that most included studies are observational (retrospective or prospective cohorts) rather than randomized interventions.\\\"]\\n\\n现有材料未提供已完成的大型随机对照 III 期临床试验证实微生物干预（如 FMT）在 ICI 治疗实体瘤中的疗效。相反，多项研究明确指出该领域仍处于早期阶段：MITRIC 试验是一项单臂 IIa 期篮子试验，结果显示在 ICI 难治性晚期癌症患者中 FMT 无客观缓解（ORR 0%），仅个别患者获得临床获益；TACITO 试验虽为随机双盲安慰剂对照试验，但仅为 IIa 期，且主要终点（12个月无进展生存率）未达到统计学显著差异（70% vs 41%, P=0.053），尽管次要终点中位 PFS 有显著改善（24.0 vs 9.0 个月, P=0.035）。此外，一项涵盖 10 项研究（164 名患者）的系统综述与荟萃分析指出，目前证据主要来自早期 Phase I/II 试验和小样本 RCT，作者明确强调“缺乏大型随机对照试验”，并呼吁进行大规模、多中心的 III 期 RCT 以确认疗效和优化方案。因此，截至这些来源的时间点，尚无完成的 III 期 RCT 确证其疗效，这一证据缺口被反复提及为当前研究的局限性及未来方向。\\n\\n现有材料未提供已完成的大型随机对照 III 期临床试验证实微生物干预（如 FMT）在 ICI 治疗实体瘤中的疗效。相反，多项研究明确指出该领域仍处于早期阶段：MITRIC 试验是一项单臂 IIa 期篮子试验，结果显示在 ICI 难治性晚期癌症患者中 FMT 无客观缓解（ORR 0%），仅个别患者获得临床获益；TACITO 试验虽为随机双盲安慰剂对照试验，但仅为 IIa 期，且主要终点（12个月无进展生存率）未达到统计学显著差异（70% vs 41%, P=0.053），尽管次要终点中位 PFS 有显著改善（24.0 vs 9.0 个月, P=0.035）。此外，一项涵盖 10 项研究（164 名患者）的系统综述与荟萃分析指出，目前证据主要来自早期 Phase I/II 试验和小样本 RCT，作者明确强调“缺乏大型随机对照试验”，并呼吁进行大规模、多中心的 III 期 RCT 以确认疗效和优化方案。因此，截至这些来源的时间点，尚无完成的 III 期 RCT 确证其疗效，这一证据缺口被反复提及为当前研究的局限性及未来方向。\\n\\n现有证据尚未证实已完成的大型随机对照 III 期临床试验能确认微生物干预在实体瘤中的疗效。目前最高级别的证据仍局限于早期阶段：MITRIC 试验是一项单臂 IIa 期篮子试验，显示在 ICI 耐药人群中 FMT 无客观缓解（ORR 0%），且微生物定植多为暂时性；一项纳入 10 项研究（164 例患者）的荟萃分析指出，尽管初步数据显示联合治疗可能有效（ pooled ORR 43%），但缺乏长期随访和大样本 RCT 数据，明确呼吁需要大型 III 期试验来验证疗效。TACITO 试验是近期发表的随机双盲安慰剂对照 IIa 期试验，虽在次要终点中位 PFS 上显示出显著获益（d-FMT 组 24.0 个月 vs p-FMT 组 9.0 个月，HR=0.50, P=0.035），但其主要终点（12 个月 PFS 率）未达到统计学显著性（70% vs 41%, P=0.053），且总生存期（OS）差异无统计学意义。因此，尽管有机制探索和 II 期阳性信号，尚无可用的 III 期确证性数据。\\nMedian Progression-Free Survival (mPFS) / TACITO trial, metastatic renal cell carcinoma (mRCC), first-line pembrolizumab + axitinib：d-FMT: 24.0 months；p-FMT: 9.0 months\",\"conditions\":[\"TACITO trial, metastatic renal cell carcinoma (mRCC), first-line pembrolizumab + axitinib\"],\"limits\":[],\"still_missing\":\"\",\"allowed_use\":[\"background_context\",\"explicit_objectives\",\"explicit_method_summaries\",\"explicit_reported_findings\",\"explicit_leads\"],\"sources\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0578\",\"paper_id\":\"d9577b3a29bd8aec60c9e27c6a56a63faf3f4a27\",\"title\":\"Safety and efficacy of fecal microbiota transplantation in solid cancers resistant to immune checkpoint inhibitors: results of the MITRIC trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1136/jitc-2026-015122\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0578\",\"paper_id\":\"d9577b3a29bd8aec60c9e27c6a56a63faf3f4a27\",\"title\":\"Safety and efficacy of fecal microbiota transplantation in solid cancers resistant to immune checkpoint inhibitors: results of the MITRIC trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1136/jitc-2026-015122\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0212\",\"paper_id\":\"5af3aee4ca5f3778325d44c8432c8b71b95ca531\",\"title\":\"Microbiota boost immunotherapy? A meta-analysis dives into fecal microbiota transplantation and immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1186/s12916-025-04183-y\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0212\",\"paper_id\":\"5af3aee4ca5f3778325d44c8432c8b71b95ca531\",\"title\":\"Microbiota boost immunotherapy? A meta-analysis dives into fecal microbiota transplantation and immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1186/s12916-025-04183-y\"},{\"paper_id\":\"69b4c5f84be199181be6ab5d3124f306462234f3\",\"title\":\"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus pembrolizumab and axitinib in metastatic renal cell carcinoma: the randomized phase 2 TACITO trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41591-025-04189-2\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"paper_id\":\"69b4c5f84be199181be6ab5d3124f306462234f3\",\"title\":\"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus pembrolizumab and axitinib in metastatic renal cell carcinoma: the randomized phase 2 TACITO trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41591-025-04189-2\",\"original_source_handle\":\"69b4c5f84be199181be6ab5d3124f306462234f3\",\"identity_status\":\"unresolved_identity\"},{\"canonical_paper_id\":\"OpenAlex:W4411127845\",\"title\":\"Microbiota boost immunotherapy? A meta-analysis dives into fecal microbiota transplantation and immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1186/s12916-025-04183-y\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_identity\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0590\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:286044272\",\"canonical_paper_id\":\"CorpusId:286044272\",\"title\":\"Gut microbiome in colorectal cancer: recent advances and clinical implications\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.3393/ac.2026.00010.0001\"},{\"canonical_paper_id\":\"OpenAlex:W3203589616\",\"title\":\"The Gut Microbiome and Cancer Immunotherapy: Can We Use the Gut Microbiome as a Predictive Biomarker for Clinical Response in Cancer Immunotherapy?\",\"year\":\"2021\",\"doi\":\"10.3390/cancers13194824\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_identity\"}],\"provenance\":{\"downloads\":0,\"model_calls\":1,\"source\":\"judge\",\"whole_paper_rereads\":0},\"chapter_ids\":[\"Ch5\"],\"unit_key\":\"\"}},{\"tool_id\":\"tool::86f40f5176043c052a8dca6749ce5e28786aa9082aac746f69d7941452e6242b\",\"value\":{\"need_id\":\"Na0b33fbc7cca9e76c1b8-5a6b848383c152a3\",\"question\":\"FMT-LUMINate 试验中 FMT 联合 ICI 的 ORR 数据是多少？供体菌群特征（如 Prevotella）与毒性（心肌炎）的关联机制是什么？\",\"intended_use\":\"mechanism\",\"decision\":\"answer_from_local\",\"usable_content\":\"FMT-LUMINate 试验是一项多中心、开放标签的 II 期研究，评估了健康供体粪便微生物群移植（FMT）联合免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）在晚期非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）或黑色素瘤患者中的疗效。在 NSCLC 队列（n=20，接受抗 PD-1 单药治疗）中，客观缓解率（ORR）为 80%；在黑色素瘤队列（n=20，接受抗 PD-1 联合抗 CTLA-4 双免疫治疗）中，ORR 为 75%。关于毒性机制，研究发现特定供体菌群特征与毒性存在情境依赖性关联：在黑色素瘤队列中，接受富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）供体 FMT 的患者出现了更高频率的严重免疫相关不良事件（irAEs），特别是心肌炎（发生率约 15%，显著高于文献报道的 <1%），且严重毒性的中位发生时间提前至 40 天（文献报道为 60 天）。这种毒性信号仅在双重免疫检查点阻断（抗 PD-1 + 抗 CTLA-4）背景下观察到，而在仅接受抗 PD-1 治疗的 NSCLC 队列或未接受该特定供体的患者中未出现，提示 Prevotella spp. 可能是双重 ICI 治疗背景下不良事件的驱动因素，强调了根据 ICI 方案背景进行供体选择的重要性。\\n：NSCLC: 80%；Melanoma: 75%\",\"conditions\":[],\"limits\":[],\"still_missing\":\"\",\"allowed_use\":[\"background_context\",\"explicit_objectives\",\"explicit_method_summaries\",\"explicit_reported_findings\",\"explicit_leads\"],\"sources\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0583\",\"paper_id\":\"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\"title\":\"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0583\",\"paper_id\":\"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\"title\":\"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\"},{\"paper_id\":\"7f830d32cd369c521fb3c16ea7dacd4444c69523\",\"title\":\"Abstract CT258: Phase II trial of fecal microbiota transplantation in combination with ipilimumab and nivolumab in patients with advanced cutaneous melanoma (FMT-LUMINate trial)\",\"year\":\"2024\",\"doi\":\"10.1158/1538-7445.am2024-ct258\",\"original_source_handle\":\"7f830d32cd369c521fb3c16ea7dacd4444c69523\",\"identity_status\":\"unresolved_identity\"},{\"paper_id\":\"7f830d32cd369c521fb3c16ea7dacd4444c69523\",\"title\":\"Abstract CT258: Phase II trial of fecal microbiota transplantation in combination with ipilimumab and nivolumab in patients with advanced cutaneous melanoma (FMT-LUMINate trial)\",\"year\":\"2024\",\"doi\":\"10.1158/1538-7445.am2024-ct258\",\"original_source_handle\":\"7f830d32cd369c521fb3c16ea7dacd4444c69523\",\"identity_status\":\"unresolved_identity\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0152\",\"paper_id\":\"43db4adf4e2779233c627e8cd307e2c0ac2ad9c1\",\"title\":\"Natural polysaccharides as immune adjuvants to overcome immune checkpoint inhibitor resistance: mechanistic insights, clinical evidence, and translational challenges\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.3389/fimmu.2026.1914914\"}],\"provenance\":{\"downloads\":0,\"model_calls\":1,\"source\":\"judge\",\"whole_paper_rereads\":0},\"chapter_ids\":[\"Ch5\"],\"unit_key\":\"\"}},{\"tool_id\":\"tool::737122dbf4b37d917d4c743b7c25100438a219fcf72bac280863b50ecf6f7279\",\"value\":{\"need_id\":\"Ndf218c8b7e158ab3c3e2-5a6b848383c152a3\",\"question\":\"MITRIC 试验中 FMT 在 ICI 耐药患者中的 ORR 及 PFS 数据是多少？为何结果为阴性？\",\"intended_use\":\"mechanism\",\"decision\":\"answer_from_local\",\"usable_content\":\"在MITRIC试验（一项针对ICI耐药晚期癌症患者的单臂IIa期篮子试验）中，FMT联合ICI治疗的客观缓解率（ORR）为0%，中位无进展生存期（PFS）仅为1.5个月，表明该干预在未经选择的耐药人群中未能产生显著的抗肿瘤疗效。尽管安全性良好且耐受性佳，但研究揭示了疗效受限的潜在机制：首先，供体微生物群在大多数受体中的定植是短暂的，仅在唯一获得临床获益（长期疾病稳定）的患者中观察到持久的定植，提示微生物群的持久整合可能是疗效的关键前提。其次，宿主免疫微环境显著影响预后，基线时髓系优势环境（高CD14+单核细胞）和高血清IL-8水平与较差的预后相关，而活化T细胞特征则与较好预后相关；然而，FMT并未显著改变外周血的免疫景观，说明其可能无法克服由宿主基础疾病状态决定的免疫抑制环境。因此，阴性结果主要归因于微生物定植的不稳定性以及宿主固有的免疫抑制状态限制了FMT的生物学效应。\\n：MITRIC_trial: ORR 0% (0/12); PFS 1.5 months; OS 10.1 months; Clinical benefit (SD >6 months) in 1 patient; irAEs in 50% of patients.\",\"conditions\":[],\"limits\":[],\"still_missing\":\"\",\"allowed_use\":[\"background_context\",\"explicit_objectives\",\"explicit_method_summaries\",\"explicit_reported_findings\",\"explicit_leads\"],\"sources\":[{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:290399336\",\"title\":\"Safety and efficacy of fecal microbiota transplantation in solid cancers resistant to immune checkpoint inhibitors: results of the MITRIC trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1136/jitc-2026-015122\",\"original_source_handle\":\"CorpusId:290399336\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_identity\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:290399336\",\"title\":\"Safety and efficacy of fecal microbiota transplantation in solid cancers resistant to immune checkpoint inhibitors: results of the MITRIC trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1136/jitc-2026-015122\",\"original_source_handle\":\"CorpusId:290399336\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_identity\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0578\",\"paper_id\":\"d9577b3a29bd8aec60c9e27c6a56a63faf3f4a27\",\"title\":\"Safety and efficacy of fecal microbiota transplantation in solid cancers resistant to immune checkpoint inhibitors: results of the MITRIC trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1136/jitc-2026-015122\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0578\",\"paper_id\":\"d9577b3a29bd8aec60c9e27c6a56a63faf3f4a27\",\"title\":\"Safety and efficacy of fecal microbiota transplantation in solid cancers resistant to immune checkpoint inhibitors: results of the MITRIC trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1136/jitc-2026-015122\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:290081712\",\"title\":\"The use of antibiotic, probiotic, and fecal microbiota transplantation in modulating immunotherapy efficacy and survival: a systematic review and meta-analysis of clinical outcomes\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1093/oncolo/oyag264\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0608\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_identity\"}],\"provenance\":{\"downloads\":0,\"model_calls\":1,\"source\":\"judge\",\"whole_paper_rereads\":0},\"chapter_ids\":[\"Ch5\"],\"unit_key\":\"\"}},{\"tool_id\":\"tool::2addc34d4cacd54826700c6f3822ed86f811a80ccbfa0ff5eed6d59d620ce6c0\",\"value\":{\"need_id\":\"N83dc9b0b1022c7adee69-6671aee87d6d5629\",\"question\":\"JCOG2007 III 期试验中肠道微生物组与 NSCLC 患者 ICI 疗效及毒性的具体关联数据是什么？\",\"intended_use\":\"mechanism\",\"decision\":\"answer_from_local\",\"usable_content\":\"现有材料中未包含 JCOG2007 III 期试验的数据。提供的文献主要涉及 FMT-LUMINate II 期试验（P0583）以及关于肠道微生物组与 ICI 疗效关联的综述（P0273, P0584）。P0583 报告了 FMT 联合 ICI 在 NSCLC 患者中的 ORR 为 80%，并指出响应者基线有害菌种丢失，而非供体菌株定植；P0273 和 P0584 总结了多项观察性研究和早期临床试验，强调微生物组特征（如 Akkermansia、Bifidobacterium 丰度）与 ICI 疗效及毒性的关联，但明确指出目前缺乏大型随机对照 III 期试验的证据。因此，无法从当前材料中提取 JCOG2007 试验的具体关联数据。\\n\\n在JCOG2007 III期试验的辅助生物标志物研究中，针对接受一线化疗联合免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗的晚期非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者，肠道微生物组组成与总生存期（OS）及严重不良事件（AEs）存在显著关联，且表现出方案特异性效应。具体而言，在尼莫鲁单抗+伊匹木单抗联合铂类双药化疗（NIC）组中，基线粪便中Fusicatenibacter和Butyricicoccus丰度较高的患者显示出更好的OS获益（相较于PC组，HR分别为0.56和0.52），且这些菌属的低丰度与发生≥4级严重不良事件的风险增加相关。相反，Prevotellaceae NK3B31的高丰度在NIC组中与更高的死亡风险相关（HR = 2.33）。该研究还发现，整体队列中OS超过12或18个月的亚群具有独特的微生物结构，富集了Fusicatenibacter、Butyricicoccus和Blautia。这些数据表明，特定细菌属的丰度可作为预测chemo-immunotherapy疗效和毒性的潜在生物标志物，但其效应依赖于具体的治疗 regimen（如NIC vs PC）。\\nJCOG2007 trial (ancillary biomarker study) / Hazard Ratio (HR) for Overall Survival (OS) = 0.56 / NIC arm (Nivolumab-ipilimumab + platinum doublet chemotherapy) vs PC arm, patients with higher abundance of Fusicatenibacter：Higher Fusicatenibacter abundance in NIC arm: HR 0.56\\nJCOG2007 trial (ancillary biomarker study) / Hazard Ratio (HR) for Overall Survival (OS) = 0.52 / NIC arm (Nivolumab-ipilimumab + platinum doublet chemotherapy) vs PC arm, patients with higher abundance of Butyricicoccus：Higher Butyricicoccus abundance in NIC arm: HR 0.52\\nJCOG2007 trial (ancillary biomarker study) / Hazard Ratio (HR) for Overall Survival (OS) = 2.33 / NIC arm (Nivolumab-ipilimumab + platinum doublet chemotherapy), patients with higher abundance of Prevotellaceae NK3B31：Higher Prevotellaceae NK3B31 abundance in NIC arm: HR 2.33\",\"conditions\":[\"JCOG2007 trial (ancillary biomarker study)\",\"NIC arm (Nivolumab-ipilimumab + platinum doublet chemotherapy) vs PC arm, patients with higher abundance of Fusicatenibacter\",\"NIC arm (Nivolumab-ipilimumab + platinum doublet chemotherapy) vs PC arm, patients with higher abundance of Butyricicoccus\",\"NIC arm (Nivolumab-ipilimumab + platinum doublet chemotherapy), patients with higher abundance of Prevotellaceae NK3B31\"],\"limits\":[],\"still_missing\":\"\",\"allowed_use\":[\"background_context\",\"explicit_objectives\",\"explicit_method_summaries\",\"explicit_reported_findings\",\"explicit_leads\"],\"sources\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0583\",\"paper_id\":\"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\"title\":\"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0583\",\"paper_id\":\"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\"title\":\"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0273\",\"paper_id\":\"759b176490dcac135bff0b645dc106c3df8f4059\",\"title\":\"The Gut Microbiome and Cancer Immunotherapy: Can We Use the Gut Microbiome as a Predictive Biomarker for Clinical Response in Cancer Immunotherapy?\",\"year\":\"2021\",\"doi\":\"10.3390/cancers13194824\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0273\",\"paper_id\":\"759b176490dcac135bff0b645dc106c3df8f4059\",\"title\":\"The Gut Microbiome and Cancer Immunotherapy: Can We Use the Gut Microbiome as a Predictive Biomarker for Clinical Response in Cancer Immunotherapy?\",\"year\":\"2021\",\"doi\":\"10.3390/cancers13194824\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:290154100\",\"title\":\"Navigating the gut–metabolite–immune axis: enhancing efficacy and mitigating toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.3389/fimmu.2026.1803970\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0584\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_identity\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0585\",\"paper_id\":\"8016df1aa5a8160b7ccd412fa6851a6a508e2731\",\"title\":\"Gut Microbiota in Advanced Non-small-cell Lung Cancer Receiving Chemo-immunotherapy: An Ancillary Biomarker Study from the Phase III trial JCOG2007 (NIPPON).\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1016/j.jtho.2025.02.026\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0417\",\"paper_id\":\"b6efedbc1ffd0d54c8ed8ce3eb0a38c148e45450\",\"title\":\"Impact of the gut microbiome on immune checkpoint inhibitor efficacy-a systematic review.\",\"year\":\"2019\",\"doi\":\"10.3747/co.26.5177\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:285298099\",\"title\":\"Engineering microbial metabolites to modulate tumor immunity and advance cancer immunotherapy\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1007/s44368-026-00019-w\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0600\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"paper_id\":\"69b4c5f84be199181be6ab5d3124f306462234f3\",\"title\":\"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus pembrolizumab and axitinib in metastatic renal cell carcinoma: the randomized phase 2 TACITO trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41591-025-04189-2\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0096\",\"paper_id\":\"261e0a3618ae7acf6e831646379929eff88857d5\",\"title\":\"The Gut Microbiome from a Biomarker to a Novel Therapeutic Strategy for Immunotherapy Response in Patients with Lung Cancer\",\"year\":\"2023\",\"doi\":\"10.3390/curroncol30110681\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0148\",\"paper_id\":\"42b8755a18f7ff2ebb90765b502a37b6f6e868e5\",\"title\":\"Response to immune checkpoint inhibition is associated with the gut microbiome in advanced KRAS-mutated non-small cell lung cancer\",\"year\":\"2023\",\"doi\":\"10.1101/2023.10.30.23297712\"},{\"paper_id\":\"c6b4401a8c45912fee23845cfc64d0fcec9315b7\",\"title\":\"Interaction of bacterial genera associated with therapeutic response to immune checkpoint PD-1 blockade in a United States cohort\",\"year\":\"2022\",\"doi\":\"10.1186/s13073-022-01037-7\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0604\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0474\",\"paper_id\":\"d227bde3dc62e02cfe87a58fa5173e149048ed4e\",\"title\":\"Tumor microenvironment-mediated resistance to immune checkpoint inhibitors in non-small cell lung cancer: Mechanisms, combination strategies and clinical perspectives (Review)\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.3892/mco.2026.2971\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0271\",\"paper_id\":\"753e796b9f6fe2fe78f1b4c6074d39441710eda7\",\"title\":\"The role of the gut microbiome on the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in Japanese responder patients with advanced non-small cell lung cancer.\",\"year\":\"2019\",\"doi\":\"10.21037/tlcr.2019.10.23\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0583\",\"paper_id\":\"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\"title\":\"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:290154100\",\"title\":\"Navigating the gut–metabolite–immune axis: enhancing efficacy and mitigating toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.3389/fimmu.2026.1803970\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0584\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_identity\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0585\",\"paper_id\":\"8016df1aa5a8160b7ccd412fa6851a6a508e2731\",\"title\":\"Gut Microbiota in Advanced Non-small-cell Lung Cancer Receiving Chemo-immunotherapy: An Ancillary Biomarker Study from the Phase III trial JCOG2007 (NIPPON).\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1016/j.jtho.2025.02.026\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:285298099\",\"title\":\"Engineering microbial metabolites to modulate tumor immunity and advance cancer immunotherapy\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1007/s44368-026-00019-w\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0600\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"paper_id\":\"69b4c5f84be199181be6ab5d3124f306462234f3\",\"title\":\"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus pembrolizumab and axitinib in metastatic renal cell carcinoma: the randomized phase 2 TACITO trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41591-025-04189-2\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0096\",\"paper_id\":\"261e0a3618ae7acf6e831646379929eff88857d5\",\"title\":\"The Gut Microbiome from a Biomarker to a Novel Therapeutic Strategy for Immunotherapy Response in Patients with Lung Cancer\",\"year\":\"2023\",\"doi\":\"10.3390/curroncol30110681\"}],\"chapter_ids\":[],\"unit_key\":\"\"}},{\"tool_id\":\"tool::17417caff54905ec019a17c3d44c8c1178fd579e1451468fc140112f2dcb2275\",\"value\":{\"need_id\":\"N48436b3aa73aea86f35f-b3c8ffc2a0ced9d8\",\"question\":\"是否有已完成的大型随机对照 III 期临床试验证实微生物干预（如 FMT）在 ICI 治疗实体瘤中的疗效？\",\"intended_use\":\"mechanism\",\"decision\":\"answer_from_local\",\"usable_content\":\"现有文献中尚未发现已完成的大型随机对照 III 期临床试验证实微生物干预（如 FMT）在实体瘤中的疗效。目前最高级别的证据来自 Phase IIa 阶段的随机对照试验和单臂研究，结果呈现异质性且未达成最终确证。\\n\\n具体而言，TACITO 试验是一项针对转移性肾细胞癌（mRCC）一线治疗患者的 Phase 2a 随机双盲安慰剂对照试验。虽然其次要终点中位无进展生存期（PFS）显著延长（24.0个月 vs 9.0个月，HR=0.50, P=0.035），但主要终点 12 个月 PFS 率未达到统计学显著差异（70% vs 41%, P=0.053），且总生存期（OS）虽呈有利趋势但未达显著性（P=0.167）。这表明在特定癌种和一线治疗背景下，FMT 显示出潜在的临床活性信号，但尚不足以作为确证性证据。\\n\\n相比之下，MITRIC 试验是一项针对多种晚期实体瘤（包括黑色素瘤、头颈鳞癌等）ICI 耐药患者的单臂 Phase IIa 篮式试验。该研究结果显示 FMT 安全性良好，但临床疗效有限：客观缓解率（ORR）为 0%，中位 PFS 仅为 1.5 个月，仅 1 名患者获得长期疾病稳定。机制分析提示，这种疗效局限可能与供体菌群定植短暂、宿主基线免疫环境（如髓系优势、高 IL-8）反映的是疾病状态而非 FMT 的直接作用有关。\\n\\n此外，Kim 等人（2024）发表的一项前瞻性单臂研究显示，在抗 PD-1 耐药的晚期实体瘤中，FMT 联合抗 PD-1 治疗可获得 7.7% 的 ORR 和 46.2% 的疾病控制率，并鉴定出特定的有益菌株（Prevotella merdae Immunoactis）。然而，由于缺乏随机对照设计和较大的样本量，这属于概念验证性质的探索性数据。\\n\\n综上所述，尽管有 Phase 2a RCT 显示部分指标改善，也有单臂研究提供机制支持，但目前缺乏大型 III 期 RCT 来确证 FMT 在广泛实体瘤人群中的确切疗效和生存获益。现有的阴性或混合结果提示疗效高度依赖于癌症类型、治疗线数（一线 vs 耐药）、供体选择及宿主免疫背景。\\nMITRIC trial (P0578) / ORR: 0%; Median PFS: 1.5 months; Clinical benefit (SD >6mo): 1/12 patients / Phase IIa single-arm basket trial, ICI-refractory advanced solid tumors (melanoma, HNSCC, RCC, MSI-H pancreatic cancer)：Total (n=12): ORR 0%, Median PFS 1.5 mo\\nTACITO trial (P0593) / 12-month PFS rate: 70% vs 41% (P=0.053); Median PFS: 24.0 vs 9.0 months (HR=0.50, P=0.035); Median OS: 41.0 vs 28.3 months (P=0.167) / Phase 2a randomized double-blind placebo-controlled trial, treatment-naive metastatic RCC (pembrolizumab + axitinib)：Donor FMT (d-FMT) (n=23 approx based on total 45): 12-mo PFS 70%, Median PFS 24.0 mo, Median OS 41.0 mo；Placebo FMT (p-FMT) (n=22 approx based on total 45): 12-mo PFS 41%, Median PFS 9.0 mo, Median OS 28.3 mo\\nKim et al. (P0594) / ORR: 7.7%; DCR: 46.2% / Prospective single-arm single-center study, anti-PD-1 refractory advanced solid cancers (gastric, esophageal, HCC)：Total (n=13): ORR 7.7%, DCR 46.2%\\n\\n截至当前材料覆盖的时间范围（主要文献发表于2024-2025年，系统综述更新至2026年中），尚无已完成的、大规模随机对照 III 期临床试验证实微生物干预（如 FMT）在 ICI 治疗实体瘤中的确切疗效。现有最高级别的临床证据为 II 期随机对照试验（RCT）。例如，TACITO 试验是一项针对转移性肾细胞癌（mRCC）患者的双盲、安慰剂对照 Phase 2a RCT，结果显示虽然中位无进展生存期（PFS）显著延长（24.0个月 vs 9.0个月，HR=0.50, P=0.035），但主要终点（12个月 PFS 率）未达到统计学显著性（70% vs 41%, P=0.053），且总生存期（OS）未显示显著差异。此外，多项单臂 II 期研究（如 MITRIC 试验在 ICI 耐药患者中 ORR 为 0%，FMT-LUMINate 试验在黑色素瘤中 ORR 为 70% 但伴随高比例严重免疫相关不良事件）提供了初步信号，但缺乏对照组验证。多篇综述明确指出，目前证据主要来自回顾性队列或早期（I/II 期）试验，亟需大规模、多中心、标准化的 III 期 RCT 来确证疗效并建立预测模型。\\n\\n[\\\"This study is a systematic review and meta-analysis (search up to September 30, 2024) that included 10 studies involving 164 patients with solid tumors treated with FMT combined with ICIs. The authors report that the included studies comprised 5 phase I trials, 4 phase II–III trials, and 3 randomized controlled trials (RCTs), but note that most were early-phase clinical trials with small sample sizes. The pooled objective response rate (ORR) was 43%, with subgroup analysis showing higher ORR (60%) for anti-PD-1 combined with anti-CTLA-4 therapy compared to monotherapy (37%). Crucially, the authors conclude in both the Abstract and Discussion that 'larger-scale randomized controlled trials with long-term follow-up are required to confirm and optimize treatment protocols' and highlight the 'absence of randomized controlled trials' (referring to large-scale/definitive ones) as a limitation. This material directly addresses the gap question by confirming that while preliminary RCT data exists, completed large-scale Phase III evidence is currently lacking and identified as a necessary future step.\\\", \\\"This review explicitly addresses the current clinical evidence level for microbiome interventions in cancer immunotherapy. The authors report that for Fecal Microbiota Transplantation (FMT), the most developed clinical evidence comes from Phase 1 studies in melanoma patients showing recovery of anti–PD-1 response in some cases. For colorectal cancer (CRC), the authors cite a Phase 2 study evaluating FMT with immunotherapy and targeted therapy that reported improvement signals but was designed without a control group, making effectiveness determination difficult. The authors conclude that large-scale prospective studies and well-designed randomized controlled trials are still needed before routine clinical use, and frame FMT in CRC as an investigational intervention rather than an established treatment.\\\", \\\"This study is a clinical review analyzing 10 studies (total n=467 patients) regarding the gut microbiome and immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) outcomes in solid tumors (melanoma, HCC, NSCLC, RCC). It reports that baseline microbiome diversity and composition (e.g., enrichment of Faecalibacterium, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) are associated with improved progression-free survival (PFS) and overall survival (OS), while Bacteroidales abundance often correlates with non-response. Crucially for the gap, the authors highlight two FMT clinical studies (Baruch et al., n=10; Davar et al., n=15) in anti-PD-1 refractory metastatic melanoma. These studies demonstrated safety and potential efficacy (30-40% response rate) when combining FMT from responders with ICI re-challenge. However, the authors explicitly state that 'further well-designed RCTs are required to explore the causal effects' and that 'future international multicentre trials will be required to provide comprehensive and reliable data.' They note that up-to-date practice guidelines based on clinical evidence are not yet available.\\\"]\\n\\n[\\\"The study provides detailed safety data (42% grade 1–2 adverse events, 37% grade 3–4 adverse events) and mechanistic hypotheses (e.g., increasing beneficial bacteria like Akkermansia muciniphila, modulating tumor microenvironment) which, while not validating the Phase III gap, offer context on why such trials are being pursued. It also notes heterogeneity in FMT protocols (donor sources, administration routes) as a barrier that large-scale trials need to standardize.\\\", \\\"The review details mechanistic pathways linking specific gut microbes to immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) response, which provides biological rationale for ongoing trials. For example, Fusobacterium nucleatum (Fn) is described as promoting immune evasion via Fap2-TIGIT binding and chemotherapy resistance, while Peptostreptococcus anaerobius (Pa) is linked to anti–PD-1 resistance via MDSC activation. Conversely, beneficial bacteria like Bifidobacterium are noted in preclinical models to enhance antitumor efficacy of PD-1 blockade. The authors also discuss confounding factors in microbiome research (e.g., stool transit time, BMI) that complicate biomarker and intervention standardization, relevant for designing future rigorous trials.\\\", \\\"The review details methodological heterogeneity across the included studies, such as variations in sequencing regions (V3-V4, V4, V4-V5), sample collection times, and cancer types, which complicates direct comparison. It also notes that only two studies examined gastrointestinal toxicity (colitis), finding low Bacteroidetes abundance associated with higher risk. The authors mention that while FMT response rates in these small studies are comparable to RCTs for Clostridioides difficile infection, the cancer FMT studies themselves are described as 'breakthrough clinical studies' rather than large-scale Phase III trials. The review excludes animal models to focus on clinical applicability but acknowledges that most included studies are observational (retrospective or prospective cohorts) rather than randomized interventions.\\\"]\\n\\n现有材料未提供已完成的大型随机对照 III 期临床试验证实微生物干预（如 FMT）在 ICI 治疗实体瘤中的疗效。相反，多项研究明确指出该领域仍处于早期阶段：MITRIC 试验是一项单臂 IIa 期篮子试验，结果显示在 ICI 难治性晚期癌症患者中 FMT 无客观缓解（ORR 0%），仅个别患者获得临床获益；TACITO 试验虽为随机双盲安慰剂对照试验，但仅为 IIa 期，且主要终点（12个月无进展生存率）未达到统计学显著差异（70% vs 41%, P=0.053），尽管次要终点中位 PFS 有显著改善（24.0 vs 9.0 个月, P=0.035）。此外，一项涵盖 10 项研究（164 名患者）的系统综述与荟萃分析指出，目前证据主要来自早期 Phase I/II 试验和小样本 RCT，作者明确强调“缺乏大型随机对照试验”，并呼吁进行大规模、多中心的 III 期 RCT 以确认疗效和优化方案。因此，截至这些来源的时间点，尚无完成的 III 期 RCT 确证其疗效，这一证据缺口被反复提及为当前研究的局限性及未来方向。\\n\\n现有材料未提供已完成的大型随机对照 III 期临床试验证实微生物干预（如 FMT）在 ICI 治疗实体瘤中的疗效。相反，多项研究明确指出该领域仍处于早期阶段：MITRIC 试验是一项单臂 IIa 期篮子试验，结果显示在 ICI 难治性晚期癌症患者中 FMT 无客观缓解（ORR 0%），仅个别患者获得临床获益；TACITO 试验虽为随机双盲安慰剂对照试验，但仅为 IIa 期，且主要终点（12个月无进展生存率）未达到统计学显著差异（70% vs 41%, P=0.053），尽管次要终点中位 PFS 有显著改善（24.0 vs 9.0 个月, P=0.035）。此外，一项涵盖 10 项研究（164 名患者）的系统综述与荟萃分析指出，目前证据主要来自早期 Phase I/II 试验和小样本 RCT，作者明确强调“缺乏大型随机对照试验”，并呼吁进行大规模、多中心的 III 期 RCT 以确认疗效和优化方案。因此，截至这些来源的时间点，尚无完成的 III 期 RCT 确证其疗效，这一证据缺口被反复提及为当前研究的局限性及未来方向。\",\"conditions\":[],\"limits\":[],\"still_missing\":\"\",\"allowed_use\":[\"background_context\",\"explicit_objectives\",\"explicit_method_summaries\",\"explicit_reported_findings\",\"explicit_leads\"],\"sources\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0578\",\"paper_id\":\"d9577b3a29bd8aec60c9e27c6a56a63faf3f4a27\",\"title\":\"Safety and efficacy of fecal microbiota transplantation in solid cancers resistant to immune checkpoint inhibitors: results of the MITRIC trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1136/jitc-2026-015122\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0578\",\"paper_id\":\"d9577b3a29bd8aec60c9e27c6a56a63faf3f4a27\",\"title\":\"Safety and efficacy of fecal microbiota transplantation in solid cancers resistant to immune checkpoint inhibitors: results of the MITRIC trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1136/jitc-2026-015122\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0212\",\"paper_id\":\"5af3aee4ca5f3778325d44c8432c8b71b95ca531\",\"title\":\"Microbiota boost immunotherapy? A meta-analysis dives into fecal microbiota transplantation and immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1186/s12916-025-04183-y\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0212\",\"paper_id\":\"5af3aee4ca5f3778325d44c8432c8b71b95ca531\",\"title\":\"Microbiota boost immunotherapy? A meta-analysis dives into fecal microbiota transplantation and immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1186/s12916-025-04183-y\"},{\"paper_id\":\"69b4c5f84be199181be6ab5d3124f306462234f3\",\"title\":\"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus pembrolizumab and axitinib in metastatic renal cell carcinoma: the randomized phase 2 TACITO trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41591-025-04189-2\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"canonical_paper_id\":\"OpenAlex:W4411127845\",\"title\":\"Microbiota boost immunotherapy? A meta-analysis dives into fecal microbiota transplantation and immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1186/s12916-025-04183-y\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_identity\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0590\",\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:286044272\",\"canonical_paper_id\":\"CorpusId:286044272\",\"title\":\"Gut microbiome in colorectal cancer: recent advances and clinical implications\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.3393/ac.2026.00010.0001\"},{\"canonical_paper_id\":\"OpenAlex:W3203589616\",\"title\":\"The Gut Microbiome and Cancer Immunotherapy: Can We Use the Gut Microbiome as a Predictive Biomarker for Clinical Response in Cancer Immunotherapy?\",\"year\":\"2021\",\"doi\":\"10.3390/cancers13194824\",\"identity_status\":\"unresolved_identity\"}],\"chapter_ids\":[],\"unit_key\":\"\"}},{\"tool_id\":\"tool::9d5fc83b8cfad5bffbda333dff7ab4b35f1c8359dada11ac3be77747c0b1e321\",\"value\":{\"need_id\":\"N61bd5cdf82bc1980ec2a-fe99d495492aaf34\",\"question\":\"是否有已完成的大型随机对照 III 期临床试验证实微生物干预（如 FMT）在 ICI 治疗实体瘤中的疗效？\",\"intended_use\":\"application_outcome\",\"decision\":\"provider_retry\",\"usable_content\":\"现有数据与用户询问的“已完成大型随机对照 III 期临床试验”设置不一致，提供的证据主要为 I/II 期研究，且研究设计（RCT vs 单臂）与人群（初治 vs 经治）存在差异。TACITO 试验（Phase 2a RCT）中，d-FMT 组相较于 p-FMT 组在 12 个月 PFS 率、中位 PFS 及中位 OS 上数值更高，提示正向差异，但原文未提供统计检验结果，不能认定具有统计学显著性。单臂试验结果方向不一致：ICI 经治人群（MITRIC 试验）ORR 为 0%，提示负向或无疗效；而初治黑色素瘤（MIMic 试验）或 NSCLC/黑色素瘤（FMT-LUMINate 试验）ORR 介于 65%-80%，提示正向差异。这表明微生物干预疗效可能受治疗线数影响，但缺乏 III 期 RCT 证实。\\n\\n适用条件：仅基于提供的 I/II 期试验数据；数值差异不代表统计显著；不包含用户指定的 III 期 RCT 证据；不推断未报告的机制。\\nTACITO trial (P0593) / 12-month PFS rate / Phase 2a RCT, mRCC, first-line：d-FMT: 70%；p-FMT: 41%\\nTACITO trial (P0593) / Median PFS / Phase 2a RCT, mRCC, first-line：d-FMT: 24.0 months；p-FMT: 9.0 months\\nTACITO trial (P0593) / Median OS / Phase 2a RCT, mRCC, first-line：d-FMT: 41.0 months；p-FMT: 28.3 months\\nMITRIC trial (P0578) / ORR / Phase IIa single-arm, ICI-refractory：All patients (n=12): 0%\\nMITRIC trial (P0578) / Median PFS / Phase IIa single-arm, ICI-refractory：All patients (n=12): 1.5 months\\nMIMic trial (P0577) / ORR / Phase I single-arm, first-line melanoma：All patients (n=20): 65%\\nMIMic trial (P0577) / Median PFS / Phase I single-arm, first-line melanoma：All patients (n=20): 29.6 months\\nFMT-LUMINate (P0583) / ORR / Phase 2 single-arm, NSCLC：NSCLC cohort: 80%\\nFMT-LUMINate (P0583) / ORR / Phase 2 single-arm, Melanoma：Melanoma cohort: 75%\",\"conditions\":[\"TACITO trial (P0593)\",\"Phase 2a RCT, mRCC, first-line\",\"MITRIC trial (P0578)\",\"Phase IIa single-arm, ICI-refractory\",\"MIMic trial (P0577)\",\"Phase I single-arm, first-line melanoma\",\"FMT-LUMINate (P0583)\",\"Phase 2 single-arm, NSCLC\",\"Phase 2 single-arm, Melanoma\"],\"limits\":[\"已完成并发表主要结局数据的 Phase III RCT 研究（如注册号为 NCT 开头的 III 期试验结果）。\"],\"still_missing\":\"已完成并发表主要结局数据的 Phase III RCT 研究（如注册号为 NCT 开头的 III 期试验结果）。\",\"allowed_use\":[\"background_context\",\"explicit_objectives\",\"explicit_method_summaries\",\"explicit_reported_findings\",\"explicit_leads\"],\"sources\":[{\"source_handle\":\"P0578\",\"paper_id\":\"d9577b3a29bd8aec60c9e27c6a56a63faf3f4a27\",\"title\":\"Safety and efficacy of fecal microbiota transplantation in solid cancers resistant to immune checkpoint inhibitors: results of the MITRIC trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1136/jitc-2026-015122\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0578\",\"paper_id\":\"d9577b3a29bd8aec60c9e27c6a56a63faf3f4a27\",\"title\":\"Safety and efficacy of fecal microbiota transplantation in solid cancers resistant to immune checkpoint inhibitors: results of the MITRIC trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1136/jitc-2026-015122\"},{\"paper_id\":\"69b4c5f84be199181be6ab5d3124f306462234f3\",\"title\":\"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus pembrolizumab and axitinib in metastatic renal cell carcinoma: the randomized phase 2 TACITO trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41591-025-04189-2\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"paper_id\":\"69b4c5f84be199181be6ab5d3124f306462234f3\",\"title\":\"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus pembrolizumab and axitinib in metastatic renal cell carcinoma: the randomized phase 2 TACITO trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41591-025-04189-2\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0593\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"paper_id\":\"a1c056e6d54a3498db16737d087fae44f686a900\",\"title\":\"Fecal microbiota transplantation improves anti-PD-1 inhibitor efficacy in unresectable or metastatic solid cancers refractory to anti-PD-1 inhibitor.\",\"year\":\"2024\",\"doi\":\"10.1016/j.chom.2024.06.010\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0594\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_handle\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0577\",\"paper_id\":\"20c143d5373eab0bfea2067cf66b0e260dfeb1ef\",\"title\":\"Improved survival in advanced melanoma patients treated with fecal microbiota transplantation using healthy donor stool in combination with anti-PD1: final results of the MIMic phase 1 trial\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1136/jitc-2025-012659\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0583\",\"paper_id\":\"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\"title\":\"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\"},{\"paper_id\":\"CorpusId:290154100\",\"title\":\"Navigating the gut–metabolite–immune axis: enhancing efficacy and mitigating toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.3389/fimmu.2026.1803970\",\"original_source_handle\":\"P0584\",\"identity_status\":\"conflicting_identity\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0577\",\"paper_id\":\"20c143d5373eab0bfea2067cf66b0e260dfeb1ef\",\"title\":\"Improved survival in advanced melanoma patients treated with fecal microbiota transplantation using healthy donor stool in combination with anti-PD1: final results of the MIMic phase 1 trial\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1136/jitc-2025-012659\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0577\",\"paper_id\":\"20c143d5373eab0bfea2067cf66b0e260dfeb1ef\",\"title\":\"Improved survival in advanced melanoma patients treated with fecal microbiota transplantation using healthy donor stool in combination with anti-PD1: final results of the MIMic phase 1 trial\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1136/jitc-2025-012659\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0577\",\"paper_id\":\"20c143d5373eab0bfea2067cf66b0e260dfeb1ef\",\"title\":\"Improved survival in advanced melanoma patients treated with fecal microbiota transplantation using healthy donor stool in combination with anti-PD1: final results of the MIMic phase 1 trial\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1136/jitc-2025-012659\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0577\",\"paper_id\":\"20c143d5373eab0bfea2067cf66b0e260dfeb1ef\",\"title\":\"Improved survival in advanced melanoma patients treated with fecal microbiota transplantation using healthy donor stool in combination with anti-PD1: final results of the MIMic phase 1 trial\",\"year\":\"2025\",\"doi\":\"10.1136/jitc-2025-012659\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0578\",\"paper_id\":\"d9577b3a29bd8aec60c9e27c6a56a63faf3f4a27\",\"title\":\"Safety and efficacy of fecal microbiota transplantation in solid cancers resistant to immune checkpoint inhibitors: results of the MITRIC trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1136/jitc-2026-015122\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0578\",\"paper_id\":\"d9577b3a29bd8aec60c9e27c6a56a63faf3f4a27\",\"title\":\"Safety and efficacy of fecal microbiota transplantation in solid cancers resistant to immune checkpoint inhibitors: results of the MITRIC trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1136/jitc-2026-015122\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0578\",\"paper_id\":\"d9577b3a29bd8aec60c9e27c6a56a63faf3f4a27\",\"title\":\"Safety and efficacy of fecal microbiota transplantation in solid cancers resistant to immune checkpoint inhibitors: results of the MITRIC trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1136/jitc-2026-015122\"},{\"source_handle\":\"P0583\",\"paper_id\":\"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\"title\":\"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\"year\":\"2026\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\"}],\"chapter_ids\":[],\"unit_key\":\"\"}}],\"source_identities\":{\"P0583\":{\"source_handle\":\"P0583\",\"source_id\":\"source::P0583\",\"aliases\":[],\"title\":\"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\"doi\":\"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\",\"paper_id\":\"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\"},\"P0577\":{\"source_handle\":\"P0577\",\"source_id\":\"source::P0577\",\"aliases\":[],\"title\":\"Improved survival in advanced melanoma patients treated with fecal microbiota transplantation using healthy donor stool in combination with anti-PD1: final results of the MIMic phase 1 trial\",\"doi\":\"10.1136/jitc-2025-012659\",\"paper_id\":\"20c143d5373eab0bfea2067cf66b0e260dfeb1ef\"},\"P0215\":{\"source_handle\":\"P0215\",\"source_id\":\"source::P0215\",\"aliases\":[],\"title\":\"Microbiome Modulation for the Treatment of Solid Neoplasms\",\"doi\":\"10.1200/jco-25-00374\",\"paper_id\":\"5b4da7a4eb5afd77f649e4aaa0b69c1db2666e97\"},\"P0343\":{\"source_handle\":\"P0343\",\"sour